    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's compute \\( 4632979^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\nWe can use the identity:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nLet\u2019s write \\( 4632979 \\) as \\( 4,600,000 + 32,979 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Square each part**\n\n- \\( a = 4,600,000 \\)\n- \\( b = 32,979 \\)\n\nFirst, \\( a^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n4,600,000^2 = (46 \\times 10^5)^2 = 46^2 \\times 10^{10}\n\\]\n\\[\n46^2 = 2116\n\\]\nSo:\n\\[\na^2 = 2116 \\times 10^{10} = 21,160,000,000,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Compute \\( 2ab \\)**\n\n\\[\n2ab = 2 \\times 4,600,000 \\times 32,979\n\\]\nFirst, \\( 4,600,000 \\times 32,979 \\):\n\nBreak \\( 4,600,000 = 46 \\times 100,000 \\):\n\n\\[\n46 \\times 32,979 = (40 + 6) \\times 32,979\n\\]\n\\[\n40 \\times 32,979 = 1,319,160\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 32,979 = 197,874\n\\]\nSum: \\( 1,319,160 + 197,874 = 1,517,034 \\)\n\nNow multiply by 100,000:\n\\[\n1,517,034 \\times 100,000 = 151,703,400,000\n\\]\nThen multiply by 2:\n\\[\n2ab = 303,406,800,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Compute \\( b^2 \\)**\n\n\\( b = 32,979 \\):\n\nLet\u2019s do \\( (33,000 - 21)^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n33,000^2 = 1,089,000,000\n\\]\n\\[\n-2 \\times 33,000 \\times 21 = -1,386,000\n\\]\n\\[\n21^2 = 441\n\\]\nSum:\n\\[\n1,089,000,000 - 1,386,000 = 1,087,614,000\n\\]\n\\[\n+ 441 = 1,087,614,441\n\\]\n\nSo \\( b^2 = 1,087,614,441 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Add them all**\n\n\\[\na^2 = 21,160,000,000,000\n\\]\n\\[\n2ab = 303,406,800,000\n\\]\n\\[\nb^2 = 1,087,614,441\n\\]\n\nFirst add \\( a^2 + 2ab \\):\n\n\\[\n21,160,000,000,000 + 303,406,800,000 = 21,463,406,800,000\n\\]\n\nNow add \\( b^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n21,463,406,800,000 + 1,087,614,441 = 21,464,494,414,441\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{21464494414441}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 21464494414441"
