{,}979)^2\\):\n\n\\(4{,}600{,}000^2 = 21{,}160{,}000{,}000{,}000\\)  \n\\(2 \\cdot 4{,}600{,}000 \\cdot 32{,}979 = 9{,}200{,}000 \\cdot 32{,}979\\).\n\n\\(32{,}979 \\cdot 9{,}200{,}000 = 32{,}979 \\cdot 92 \\times 10^5\\).\n\n\\(32{,}979 \\cdot 92 = 32{,}979 \\cdot (100 - 8) = 3{,}297{,}900 - 263{,}832 = 3{,}034{,}068\\).\n\nMultiply by \\(10^5\\): \\(303{,}406{,}800{,}000\\).\n\nNow \\(32{,}979^2\\):\n\n\\((33{,}000 - 21)^2 = 1{,}089{,}000{,}000 - 1{,}386{,}000 + 441 = 1{,}087{,}614{,}441\\).\n\nSum:\n\n\\(21{,}160{,}000{,}000{,}000 + 303{,}406{,}800{,}000 = 21{,}463{,}406{,}800{,}000\\).  \nAdd \\(1{,}087{,}614{,}441\\): \\(21{,}464{,}494{,}414{,}441\\).\n\nThis does **not** match my first result \u2014 so I made an error somewhere. Let's check the first approach again.\n\nOh \u2014 I see: in the first method, \\(a = 4{,}630{,}000\\), \\(b = 2{,}979\\), but \\(4{,}630{,}000 + 2{,}979 = 4{,}632{,}979\\) \u2014 correct.\n\nCheck \\(a^2\\): \\(4{,}630{,}000^2\\) = \\((463 \\times 10^4)^2\\) = \\(463^2 \\times 10^8\\).\n\n\\(463^2 = (460+3)^2 = 211{,}600 + 2{,}760 + 9 = 214{,}369\\).\n\nMultiply by \\(10^8\\): \\(21{,}436{,}900{,}000{,}000\\) \u2014 yes.\n\n\\(2ab\\): \\(2 \\cdot 4{,}630{,}000 \\cdot 2{,}979\\):\n\n\\(4{,}630{,}000 \\cdot 2{,}979 = 4{,}630{,}000 \\cdot (3000 - 21)\\)  \n= \\(13{,}890{,}000{,}000 - 97{,}230{,}000 = 13{,}792{,}770{,}000\\) \u2014 correct.  \nDouble: \\(27{,}585{,}540{,}000\\) \u2014 yes.\n\n\\(b^2 = 2{,}979^2 = 8{,}874{,}441\\) \u2014 correct.\n\nSubtract: \\(21{,}436{,}900{,}000{,}000 - 27{,}585{,}540{,}000\\):\n\n\\(21{,}436{,}900{,}000{,}000 - 27{,}000{,}000{,}000 = 21{,}409{,}900{,}000{,}000\\)  \nThen subtract \\(585{,}540{,}000\\) = \\(21{,}409{,}314{,}460{,}000\\) \u2014 yes.\n\nAdd \\(8{,}874{,}441\\) = \\(21{,}409{,}323{,}334{,}441\\).\n\nSo the first answer is \\(21{,}409{,}323{,}334{,}441\\).\n\nThe second check must have an error \u2014 probably in \\(4{,}600{,}000^2\\).\n\n\\(4{,}600{,}000^2 = (46 \\times 10^5)^2 = 2116 \\t