 step-by-step.\n\nWe need the remainder when \\( 6799523635 \\) is divided by \\( 898 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Break the problem using modular arithmetic.**\n\nWe want \\( 6799523635 \\mod 898 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\( 898 = 2 \\times 449 \\).  \nWe can compute mod 898 directly using long division or modular reduction.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Use the fact that \\( 1000 \\equiv 102 \\pmod{898} \\) since \\( 1000 - 898 = 102 \\).**\n\nLet's write \\( 6799523635 \\) in chunks of 3 digits (base 1000):\n\n\\( 6,799,523,635 \\) = \\( 6 \\times 1000^3 + 799 \\times 1000^2 + 523 \\times 1000 + 635 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Work modulo 898.**\n\nWe have:\n\n- \\( 1000 \\equiv 102 \\pmod{898} \\).\n- \\( 1000^2 \\equiv 102^2 = 10404 \\).  \nNow reduce 10404 mod 898:  \n\\( 898 \\times 11 = 9878 \\), remainder \\( 10404 - 9878 = 526 \\).  \nSo \\( 1000^2 \\equiv 526 \\).\n\n- \\( 1000^3 \\equiv 526 \\times 102 = 53652 \\).  \nReduce mod 898:  \n\\( 898 \\times 59 = 52982 \\), remainder \\( 53652 - 52982 = 670 \\).  \nSo \\( 1000^3 \\equiv 670 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Compute each term.**\n\nTerm 1: \\( 6 \\times 670 = 4020 \\).  \nReduce: \\( 898 \\times 4 = 3592 \\), remainder \\( 4020 - 3592 = 428 \\).\n\nTerm 2: \\( 799 \\times 526 \\).  \nFirst, \\( 800 \\times 526 = 420800 \\), subtract \\( 1 \\times 526 = 526 \\), get \\( 420274 \\).  \nReduce mod 898:  \n\\( 898 \\times 468 = 420264 \\) (since \\( 898 \\times 400 = 359200 \\), plus \\( 898 \\times 68 = 61064 \\) \u2192 total 420264).  \nRemainder \\( 420274 - 420264 = 10 \\).\n\nTerm 3: \\( 523 \\times 102 = 53346 \\).  \nReduce: \\( 898 \\times 59 = 52982 \\), remainder \\( 53346 - 52982 = 364 \\).\n\nTerm 4: \\( 635 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Sum the remainders.**\n\n\\( 428 + 10 + 364 + 635 = 1437 \\).\n\nReduce \\( 1437 \\mod 898 \\):  \n\\( 1437 - 898 = 539 \\).\n\nSo remainder is \\( 539 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 6: Double-check with mod 2 and mod 449.**\n\nMod 2: number is odd \u2192 remainder mod 2 = 1.  \n539 mod 2 = 1, matches.\n\nMod 449:  \nWe can check 539 mod 449 = 90.  \nTo verify original number mod 449 quickly:  \nUse 1000 \u2261 102 mod 449:  \n1000 \u2261 102,  \n1000^2 \u2261 102^2 = 10404 mod 449: 449\u00d723=10327, remainder 77.  \n1000^3 \u2261 77\u00d7102 = 7854 mod 449: 449\u00d717=7633, remainder 221.\n\nTerms:  \n6\u00d7221=1326 mod 449: 449\u00d72=898, remainder 428.  \n799\u00d777: 800\u00d777=61600 minus 77=61523, mod 449: 449\u00d7137=61513, remainder 10.  \n523\u00d7102=53346 mod 449: 449\u00d7118=52982, remainder 364.  \n+635.\n\nSum: 428+10+364+635=1437, mod 449: 449\u00d73=1347, remainder 90. Matches 539 mod 449 = 90. Good.\n\n---\n\n**Step 7: Check uniqueness mod 898.**  \nRemainder must be < 898 and match mod 2=1, mod 449=90.  \nThe number 539 satisfies 539 mod 2=1, mod 449=90. The other candidate would be 539+449=988>898, so 539 is correct.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nAnswer: 539  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's calculate step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 6799523635 \\) is divided by \\( 898 \\).\n\nFirst, note:  \n\\( 898 = 2 \\times 449 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Modulo 2**  \n\\( 6799523635 \\) is odd, so remainder mod 2 is 1.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Modulo 449**  \nWe can reduce the large number mod 449.\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\( 6799523635 \\mod 449 \\).\n\nFirst, notice \\( 449 \\times 15,000,000 = 6,735,000,000 \\).  \nDifference:  \n\\( 6,799,523,635 - 6,735,000,000 = 64,523,635 \\).\n\nNow reduce 64,523,635 mod 449.\n\n\\( 449 \\times 143,000 = 64,207,000 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 64,523,635 - 64,207,000 = 316,635 \\).\n\n\\( 449 \\times 700 = 314,300 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 316,635 - 314,300 = 2,335 \\).\n\n\\( 449 \\times 5 = 2,245 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 2,335 - 2,245 = 90 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 449 is 90.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Combine via Chinese Remainder Theorem**  \nWe have:  \n\\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 90 \\pmod{449} \\)\n\nSince 90 is even, it\u2019s not \u22611 mod 2. So add 449 (which is odd) repeatedly until mod 2 matches:\n\n\\( 90 + 449 = 539 \\) (odd) \u2192 mod 2 = 1. Good.\n\nCheck: 539 < 898, so that\u2019s the remainder mod 898.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Verify**  \n539 mod 898 is less than 898.  \nCheck mod 2: 539 is odd, remainder 1. \u2713  \nCheck mod 449: 539 - 449 = 90. \u2713\n\nSo remainder is 539.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 539  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nLet's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 6799523635 \\) is divided by \\( 898 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Estimate quotient**\n\nWe can do long division or modular arithmetic. I\u2019ll do modular reduction.\n\nFirst, note:\n\\( 898 = 2 \\times 449 \\), but since 6799523635 is odd, mod 2 is 1. But better to work directly mod 898.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Break the number into parts**\n\nWe can compute \\( 6799523635 \\mod 898 \\) using stepwise reduction.\n\nWe know:\n\\( 898 \\times 7,\\!000,\\!000 = 6,\\!286,\\!000,\\!000 \\)  \nDifference:  \n\\( 6,\\!799,\\!523,\\!635 - 6,\\!286,\\!000,\\!000 = 513,\\!523,\\!635 \\).  \nSo \\( 6799523635 \\equiv 513523635 \\pmod{898} \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Reduce 513,523,635 mod 898**\n\nWe can find how many times 898 fits into 513,523,635.\n\nFirst, 898 \u00d7 500,000 = 449,000,000.  \nRemainder: 513,523,635 \u2212 449,000,000 = 64,523,635.\n\n898 \u00d7 70,000 = 62,860,000.  \nRemainder: 64,523,635 \u2212 62,860,000 = 1,663,635.\n\n898 \u00d7 1,800 = 1,616,400.  \nRemainder: 1,663,635 \u2212 1,616,400 = 47,235.\n\n898 \u00d7 50 = 44,900.  \nRemainder: 47,235 \u2212 44,900 = 2,335.\n\n898 \u00d7 2 = 1,796.  \nRemainder: 2,335 \u2212 1,796 = 539.\n\n539 < 898, so final remainder is 539.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Check quickly**\n\nSo \\( 6799523635 \\mod 898 = 539 \\).\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 539  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go through this step by step.\n\nWe need the remainder when \\( 6799523635 \\) is divided by \\( 898 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Modulo approach**\n\nLet's first approximate.\n\n\\( 898 \\times 7,500,000 = 6,735,000,000 \\) \