    "raw": "Let's compute the remainder of \\( 6540804836 \\div 568 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 568 = 8 \\times 71 \\).  \nWe can find the remainder modulo 568 by using the division algorithm.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Estimate quotient**  \n568 \u00d7 10,000,000 = 5,680,000,000, which is less than 6,540,804,836.  \nDifference: 6,540,804,836 \u2212 5,680,000,000 = 860,804,836.\n\n568 \u00d7 1,000,000 = 568,000,000.  \n860,804,836 \u2212 568,000,000 = 292,804,836.\n\n568 \u00d7 500,000 = 284,000,000.  \n292,804,836 \u2212 284,000,000 = 8,804,836.\n\n568 \u00d7 15,000 = 8,520,000.  \n8,804,836 \u2212 8,520,000 = 284,836.\n\n568 \u00d7 500 = 284,000.  \n284,836 \u2212 284,000 = 836.\n\n568 \u00d7 1 = 568.  \n836 \u2212 568 = 268.\n\nSo quotient so far: 10,000,000 + 1,000,000 + 500,000 + 15,000 + 500 + 1 = 11,515,501.  \nRemainder = 268.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Check**  \n568 \u00d7 11,515,501 = 568 \u00d7 (11,500,000 + 15,501)  \n= 6,532,000,000 + (568 \u00d7 15,501).  \n568 \u00d7 15,501 = 568 \u00d7 15,000 + 568 \u00d7 501 = 8,520,000 + 284,568 = 8,804,568.  \nSum: 6,532,000,000 + 8,804,568 = 6,540,804,568.  \nAdd remainder 268 \u2192 6,540,804,836. Correct.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nAnswer: 268  \nConfidence: 100%"
