    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 6540804836 \\) is divided by \\( 568 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Check divisibility and simplify if possible.**\n\nFirst, note \\( 568 = 8 \\times 71 \\).  \nWe can find the remainder mod 8 and mod 71, then combine.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 8.**\n\nA number mod 8 depends only on its last 3 digits.\n\nLast 3 digits of \\( 6540804836 \\) are \\( 836 \\).\n\n\\( 836 \\div 8 = 104\\) remainder \\(4\\) (since \\(8 \\times 104 = 832\\), remainder \\(4\\)).\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\n6540804836 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Mod 71.**\n\nWe can do this by breaking the number or using modular reduction.\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\( 6540804836 \\mod 71 \\).\n\nFirst, \\( 71 \\times 92124011 = ? \\) \u2014 maybe easier to do stepwise.\n\nLet\u2019s use the fact \\(10^3 = 1000 \\equiv 1000 - 71\\times14 = 1000 - 994 = 6 \\pmod{71}\\).\n\nSo \\(10^3 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{71}\\).\n\nWrite \\( 6540804836 \\) in base 1000:\n\n- Group digits from right in threes:  \n\\( 6,540,804,836 \\) \u2192 groups: \\(6\\) | \\(540\\) | \\(804\\) | \\(836\\).\n\nActually check: 6,540,804,836 \u2192 groups: 6 | 540 | 804 | 836. Yes.\n\nSo:\n\n\\( N = 6\\times 1000^3 + 540\\times 1000^2 + 804\\times 1000 + 836\\).\n\nMod 71, \\(1000 \\equiv 6\\).\n\nThus:\n\n\\(1000^2 \\equiv 6^2 = 36\\)  \n\\(1000^3 \\equiv 6^3 = 216 \\equiv 216 - 71\\times3 = 216 - 213 = 3\\).\n\nSo:\n\n\\(N \\equiv 6\\times 3 + 540\\times 36 + 804\\times 6 + 836 \\pmod{71}\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Reduce each term mod 71.**\n\n- First term: \\(6\\times 3 = 18\\).\n\n- Second term: \\(540\\times 36\\).  \nFirst \\(540 \\mod 71\\): \\(71\\times 7=497\\), remainder \\(540-497=43\\).  \nThen \\(43\\times 36 = 1548\\).  \n\\(1548 \\mod 71\\): \\(71\\times 21=1491\\), remainder \\(1548-1491=57\\).\n\n- Third term: \\(804\\times 6\\).  \n\\(804 \\mod 71\\): \\(71\\times 11=781\\), remainder \\(23\\).  \n\\(23\\times 6=138\\).  \n\\(138 \\mod 71 = 138 - 71 = 67\\).\n\n- Fourth term: \\(836 \\mod 71\\): \\(71\\times 11=781\\), remainder \\(55\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Sum them mod 71.**\n\nSum: \\(18 + 57 = 75\\), plus \\(67\\) = \\(142\\), plus \\(55\\) = \\(197\\).\n\n\\(197 \\mod 71\\): \\(71\\times 2=142\\), remainder \\(55\\).\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\nN \\equiv 55 \\pmod{71}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 6: Solve system.**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\[\nx \\equiv 4 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 55 \\pmod{71}\n\\]\n\nLet \\(x = 55 + 71k\\).  \nMod 8: \\(55 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}\\), \\(71 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}\\).\n\nSo \\(7 + 7k \\equiv 4 \\pmod{8}\\).  \nThus \\(7k \\equiv -3 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{8}\\).\n\nMultiply inverse of 7 mod 8: \\(7^{-1} \\equiv 7\\) (since \\(7\\times 7=49\\equiv 1\\)).\n\nSo \\(k \\equiv 5\\times 7 = 35 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{8}\\).\n\nSmallest \\(k=3\\).\n\nThen \\(x = 55 + 71\\times 3 = 55 + 213 = 268\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 7: Check range.**\n\n\\(268 < 568\\), so remainder is \\(268\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 8: Quick check.**\n\n\\(6540804836 - 268 = 6540804568\\). Divide by 568:  \n\\(568\\times 11515430 = ?\\) Let's check mod:  \n568\u00d711,515,430 = 568\u00d7(11,500,000 + 15,430) = 6,532,000,000 + 8,764,240 = 6,540,764,240. Wait, that\u2019s not matching \u2014 let's check more carefully.\n\nActually, better check: 568\u00d711,515,430:  \n568\u00d711,000,000 = 6,248,000,000  \n568\u00d7515,430 = 568\u00d7500,000=284,000,000; plus 568\u00d715,430=8,764,240. Sum: 284,000,000+8,764,240=292,764,240.  \nTotal: 6,248,000,000 + 292,764,240 = 6,540,764,240. Yes, that\u2019s correct.\n\nOur number is 6,540,804,836. Difference: 6,540,804,836 - 6,540,764,240 = 40,596.  \n40,596 \u00f7 568 = 71.47..., not integer. So maybe my check multiplier was wrong.\n\nLet\u2019s instead check 268 mod 8 = 4 (yes), mod 71: 268 - 71\u00d73=268-213=55 (yes). So correct.\n\n---\n\nFinal answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{268}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 268"
