    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 7001003053 \\) is divided by \\( 456 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Break down the divisor**\n\n\\( 456 = 8 \\times 57 = 8 \\times 3 \\times 19 \\).\n\nWe could use the Chinese Remainder Theorem, but since 8, 3, and 19 are pairwise coprime, we can find the remainder mod 456 by finding remainders mod 8, mod 3, and mod 19, then combining.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Mod 8**\n\nA number mod 8 depends only on its last 3 digits.\n\nLast 3 digits of \\( 7001003053 \\) are \\( 053 \\) \u2192 53.\n\n\\( 53 \\div 8 = 6\\) remainder \\(5\\).\n\nSo remainder mod 8 = 5.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Mod 3**\n\nSum of digits: \\( 7+0+0+1+0+0+3+0+5+3 = 19 \\).\n\n\\( 19 \\mod 3 = 1 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 3 = 1.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Mod 19**\n\nWe can do this by breaking the number or using modular reduction.\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\( 7001003053 \\mod 19 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\( 10^3 = 1000 \\), and \\( 1000 \\mod 19 \\):\n\n\\( 19 \\times 52 = 988\\), remainder \\(12\\). So \\(10^3 \\equiv 12 \\pmod{19}\\).\n\nBut maybe easier: process digits.\n\nLet\u2019s do stepwise:\n\nStart with remainder 0.\n\n- Digit 7: \\(0\\times 10 + 7 = 7\\) \u2192 7 mod 19 = 7.\n- Next digit 0: \\(7\\times 10 + 0 = 70\\), 70 mod 19: 19\u00d73=57, remainder 13.\n- Next digit 0: \\(13\\times 10 + 0 = 130\\), 130 mod 19: 19\u00d76=114, remainder 16.\n- Next digit 1: \\(16\\times 10 + 1 = 161\\), 161 mod 19: 19\u00d78=152, remainder 9.\n- Next digit 0: \\(9\\times 10 + 0 = 90\\), 90 mod 19: 19\u00d74=76, remainder 14.\n- Next digit 0: \\(14\\times 10 + 0 = 140\\), 140 mod 19: 19\u00d77=133, remainder 7.\n- Next digit 3: \\(7\\times 10 + 3 = 73\\), 73 mod 19: 19\u00d73=57, remainder 16.\n- Next digit 0: \\(16\\times 10 + 0 = 160\\), 160 mod 19: 19\u00d78=152, remainder 8.\n- Next digit 5: \\(8\\times 10 + 5 = 85\\), 85 mod 19: 19\u00d74=76, remainder 9.\n- Next digit 3: \\(9\\times 10 + 3 = 93\\), 93 mod 19: 19\u00d74=76, remainder 17.\n\nSo remainder mod 19 = 17.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Combine using CRT**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\( x \\equiv 5 \\pmod{8} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 17 \\pmod{19} \\)\n\nFirst combine mod 8 and mod 3 (mod 24):\n\nNumbers \u2261 5 mod 8: 5, 13, 21, \u2026  \nCheck mod 3:  \n5 mod 3 = 2 (no),  \n13 mod 3 = 1 (yes). So \\( x \\equiv 13 \\pmod{24} \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 6 \u2013 Combine with mod 19**\n\nWe want \\( x \\equiv 13 \\pmod{24} \\) and \\( x \\equiv 17 \\pmod{19} \\).\n\nLet \\( x = 13 + 24k \\).  \nMod 19: \\( 13 + 24k \\equiv 17 \\pmod{19} \\).\n\n24 mod 19 = 5, so \\( 13 + 5k \\equiv 17 \\pmod{19} \\).  \nThus \\( 5k \\equiv 4 \\pmod{19} \\).\n\nFind inverse of 5 mod 19:  \n5\u00d74=20\u22611, so inverse is 4.\n\nMultiply: \\( k \\equiv 4\u00d74 = 16 \\pmod{19} \\).\n\nSmallest k = 16.\n\nThen \\( x = 13 + 24\u00d716 = 13 + 384 = 397 \\).\n\nSince 397 < 456, that\u2019s the remainder.\n\n---\n\n**Step 7 \u2013 Check**\n\n397 mod 8 = 5 \u2714  \n397 mod 3 = 1 \u2714  \n397 mod 19: 19\u00d720=380, remainder 17 \u2714.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\n\nAnswer: 397"
