= 3+9+7=19 \u2192 1 mod 3 \u2705.\n\nMod 19: 7001003053 mod 19:  \n19 \u00d7 368,473,845 = 7,001,003,055, which is 2 too big, so remainder is -2 \u2261 17 mod 19.  \n397 mod 19: 19\u00d720=380, remainder 17 \u2705.\n\nEverything matches.\n\n**Final Answer:** 397.\n\nAnswer: 397  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nAlright, let's go through it step-by-step.  \n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 7001003053 \\) is divided by \\( 456 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Break down the modulus**  \n\\( 456 = 8 \\times 57 \\)  \nand \\( 57 = 3 \\times 19 \\).  \nSo \\( 456 = 2^3 \\times 3 \\times 19 \\).  \nWe could solve using Chinese Remainder Theorem (mod 8, mod 3, mod 19), but since 456 is not too big, we can also do direct division.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Try direct modular reduction**  \nWe can do this by breaking the big number into manageable chunks.\n\nFirst, note \\( 1000 \\mod 456 \\):  \n\\( 456 \\times 2 = 912\\), remainder \\(1000 - 912 = 88\\).  \nSo \\( 1000 \\equiv 88 \\pmod{456} \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Express the number in base 1000**  \n\\( 7001003053 = 7 \\times 1000^3 + 1 \\times 1000^2 + 3 \\times 1000 + 53 \\)? Wait, let's check grouping:\n\nFrom the right:  \n- Last 3 digits: 053 \u2192 53  \n- Next 3 digits: 003 \u2192 3  \n- Next 3 digits: 001 \u2192 1  \n- Next: 7  \n\nYes, correct grouping: \\( 7|001|003|053 \\)  \nSo the number is \\( 7 \\times 1000^3 + 1 \\times 1000^2 + 3 \\times 1000 + 53 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Reduce powers of 1000 mod 456**  \nWe have \\( 1000 \\equiv 88 \\pmod{456} \\).\n\n- \\( 1000^2 \\mod 456 \\):  \nFirst, \\( 88^2 = 7744 \\).  \nDivide 7744 by 456: \\( 456 \\times 16 = 7296 \\), remainder \\( 7744 - 7296 = 448 \\).  \n448 \u2261 -8 mod 456. So \\( 1000^2 \\equiv 448 \\).\n\n- \\( 1000^3 \\mod 456 \\):  \n\\( 448 \\times 88 = 39424 \\).  \nDivide by 456: \\( 456 \\times 86 = 39216\\), remainder \\( 39424 - 39216 = 208\\).  \nSo \\( 1000^3 \\equiv 208 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Compute the value**  \nTerm1: \\( 7 \\times 208 = 1456 \\).  \n1456 mod 456: \\( 456 \\times 3 = 1368\\), remainder \\(1456 - 1368 = 88\\).\n\nTerm2: \\( 1 \\times 448 = 448\\).\n\nTerm3: \\( 3 \\times 88 = 264\\).\n\nTerm4: \\(53\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 6: Sum them**  \nSum = \\(88 + 448 + 264 + 53\\).  \n88 + 448 = 536.  \n536 + 264 = 800.  \n800 + 53 = 853.\n\n---\n\n**Step 7: Final mod**  \n853 mod 456: \\( 853 - 456 = 397\\).\n\nSo the remainder is 397.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 397  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nLet's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want:  \n\\( 7001003053 \\mod 456 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Break down 456.**  \n\\( 456 = 8 \\times 57 = 8 \\times 3 \\times 19 \\).\n\nSo we could use the Chinese Remainder Theorem with mod 8, mod 3, and mod 19.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 8.**  \nLast three digits of 7001003053 are 053 \u2192 53.  \n\\( 53 \\mod 8 = 5\\).  \nSo remainder mod 8 = 5.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Mod 3.**  \nSum of digits of 7001003053:  \n7+0+0+1+0+0+3+0+5+3 = 19.  \n19 mod 3 = 1.  \nSo remainder mod 3 = 1.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Mod 19.**  \nWe can do this by reducing step-by-step.\n\nFirst note: \\(10^3 = 1000\\), and \\(1000 \\mod 19\\):  \n19\u00d752 = 988, remainder 12. So \\(10^3 \\equiv 12 \\pmod{19}\\).  \nBut maybe easier to just do direct long mod.\n\nLet\u2019s compute 7001003053 mod 19.\n\nStart with 0.\n\n- Bring down 7 \u2192 7.  \n7 mod 19 = 7.\n\n- Next digit 0: 7\u00d710 + 0 = 70 \u2192 70 mod 19: 19\u00d73=57, remainder 13.\n\n- Next digit 0: 13\u00d710 + 0 = 130 \u2192 130 mod 19: 19\u00d76=114, remainder 16.\n\n- Next digit 1: 16\u00d710 + 1 = 161 \u2192 161 mod 19: 19\u00d78=152, remainder 9.\n\n- Next digit 0: 9\u00d710 + 0 = 90 \u2192 90 mod 19: 19\u00d74=76, remainder 14.\n\n- Next digit 0: 14\u00d710 + 0 = 140 \u2192 140 mod 19: 19\u00d77=133, remainder 7.\n\n- Next digit 3: 7\u00d710 + 3 = 73 \u2192 73 mod 19: 19\u00d73=57, remainder 16.\n\n- Next digit 0: 16\u00d710 + 0 = 160 \u2192 160 mod 19: 19\u00d78=152, remainder 8.\n\n- Next digit 5: 8\u00d710 + 5 = 85 \u2192 85 mod 19: 19\u00d74=76, remainder 9.\n\n- Ne