uping: write the number in 3-digit chunks from the right:\n\n7,001,003,053 \u2192 chunks: 7 | 001 | 003 | 053.  \nMeaning: \\( 7 \\times 1000^3 + 1 \\times 1000^2 + 3 \\times 1000 + 53 \\) (check: 1 is 001, 3 is 003, 53 is 053).\n\nNow 1000 \u2261 12 (mod 19):\n\n- 1000^2 \u2261 12^2=144 \u2261 144-19\u00d77=144-133=11 mod 19.\n- 1000^3 \u2261 12\u00d711=132 \u2261 132-19\u00d76=132-114=18 mod 19.\n\nNow compute:\n\nTerm1: 7\u00d718 = 126 \u2261 126 - 19\u00d76=126-114=12.  \nTerm2: 1\u00d711 = 11.  \nTerm3: 3\u00d712 = 36 \u2261 36-19=17.  \nTerm4: 53 \u2261 53-38=15.\n\nSum: 12 + 11 = 23 \u2261 4, +17=21 \u2261 2, +15=17.\n\nSo mod 19 = 17.\n\n---\n\nNow we have:\n\n- x \u2261 5 mod 8  \n- x \u2261 1 mod 3  \n- x \u2261 17 mod 19  \n\nSince 8, 3, 19 are pairwise coprime, use CRT.\n\nFirst combine mod 8 and mod 3:\n\nx \u2261 5 mod 8, x \u2261 1 mod 3.\n\nList x \u2261 5 mod 8: 5, 13, 21, 29, ... check mod 3:  \n5 mod 3=2, 13 mod 3=1 \u2192 matches. So x \u2261 13 mod 24.\n\nNow combine with mod 19:\n\nx \u2261 13 mod 24, x \u2261 17 mod 19.\n\nLet x = 13 + 24k.  \n13 + 24k \u2261 17 mod 19.  \n24 mod 19 = 5, so 13 + 5k \u2261 17 mod 19 \u2192 5k \u2261 4 mod 19.\n\nFind inverse of 5 mod 19: 5\u00d74=20\u22611, so inverse is 4.  \nk \u2261 4\u00d74=16 mod 19.\n\nSmallest k=16: x=13 + 24\u00d716 = 13 + 384 = 397.\n\nCheck 397 mod 456 is just 397 (since less than 456), but is that the remainder? Yes.\n\nCheck:\n\n- 397 mod 8: 8\u00d749=392, remainder 5 \u2714  \n- 397 mod 3: 3\u00d7132=396, remainder 1 \u2714  \n- 397 mod 19: 19\u00d720=380, remainder 17 \u2714\n\nSo remainder is 397.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer**:  \nAnswer: 397  \nConfidence: 95%"
