    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 26511507 \\) is divided by \\( 196 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Check divisibility and simplify if possible.**\n\nFirst, note \\(196 = 14^2 = 4 \\times 49 = 2^2 \\times 7^2\\).\n\nWe can find the remainder mod 196 by finding it mod 4 and mod 49, then using the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 4.**\n\nA number mod 4 depends on its last two digits.\n\nLast two digits of \\(26511507\\) are \\(07\\), which is \\(7\\).\n\n\\(7 \\mod 4 = 3\\).\n\nSo remainder mod 4 is 3.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Mod 49.**\n\nWe need \\(26511507 \\mod 49\\).\n\nFirst, reduce 26511507 mod 49.\n\nLet's do it stepwise:\n\n- \\(49 \\times 500000 = 24500000\\).  \n  Subtract: \\(26511507 - 24500000 = 2011507\\).\n\n- \\(49 \\times 40000 = 1960000\\).  \n  Subtract: \\(2011507 - 1960000 = 51507\\).\n\n- \\(49 \\times 1000 = 49000\\).  \n  Subtract: \\(51507 - 49000 = 2507\\).\n\n- \\(49 \\times 50 = 2450\\).  \n  Subtract: \\(2507 - 2450 = 57\\).\n\n- \\(49 \\times 1 = 49\\).  \n  Subtract: \\(57 - 49 = 8\\).\n\nSo remainder mod 49 is 8.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Solve system.**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\[\nx \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 8 \\pmod{49}\n\\]\n\nFrom the second: \\(x = 8 + 49k\\).\n\nPlug into first: \\(8 + 49k \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}\\).\n\n49 mod 4 = 1, so \\(8 + k \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}\\).\n\n8 mod 4 = 0, so \\(k \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}\\).\n\nSmallest \\(k = 3\\).\n\nThen \\(x = 8 + 49 \\times 3 = 8 + 147 = 155\\).\n\nCheck: 155 mod 4 = 3, 155 mod 49 = 8. Good.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Conclusion.**\n\nThe remainder is \\(155\\).\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 155"
