= 8 + 49k \\).\n\nCheck mod 4: \\( 8 \\equiv 0 \\), \\( 49 \\equiv 1 \\) mod 4.  \nSo \\( 0 + 1k \\equiv 3 \\) mod 4 \u2192 \\( k \\equiv 3 \\) mod 4.\n\nSmallest \\( k = 3 \\):  \n\\( x = 8 + 49 \\times 3 = 8 + 147 = 155 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Check**  \n155 mod 4 = 3 \u2705  \n155 mod 49 = 155 - 49\u00d73 = 155 - 147 = 8 \u2705  \nAlso 155 < 196, so remainder is 155.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 155  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet\u2019s go step-by-step.\n\nWe need the remainder of \\( 26511507 \\) divided by \\( 196 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Factor modulus**  \n\\( 196 = 4 \\times 49 = 4 \\times 7^2 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder modulo \\( 196 \\) directly by division, but knowing it\u2019s \\( 4 \\times 49 \\) can help check.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Direct division**  \n\nFirst, approximate:  \n\\( 196 \\times 135000 = 196 \\times 135000 \\). Let\u2019s break it:\n\n\\( 196 \\times 100,000 = 19,600,000 \\)  \n\\( 196 \\times 35,000 = 6,860,000 \\)  \nSum = \\( 26,460,000 \\).\n\nOur number: \\( 26,511,507 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 26,511,507 - 26,460,000 = 51,507 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Divide remainder further**  \n\n\\( 196 \\times 262 = 196 \\times 260 + 196 \\times 2 \\)  \n\\( 196 \\times 260 = 50,960 \\)  \nPlus \\( 392 \\) = \\( 51,352 \\).\n\nDifference: \\( 51,507 - 51,352 = 155 \\).\n\n155 < 196, so remainder is 155.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Check with modular arithmetic**  \n\nMod 4: 26511507 mod 4: last two digits 07 \u2192 7 mod 4 = 3.  \n155 mod 4 = 3 \u2713.\n\nMod 49: 26511507 mod 49:  \nFirst mod 7: 26511507 \u2192 sum digits? Actually easier: divide by 7:  \n7 \u00d7 3,787,358 = 26,511,506, remainder 1. So mod 7 = 1.\n\nNow mod 49: Let\u2019s compute using 196 method is fine; but check: 155 mod 49 = 155 - 3\u00d749 = 155 - 147 = 8.  \nSo check if 26511507 mod 49 = 8?  \n\nWe can check mod 49:  \nNote 10^3 = 1000 \u2261 1000 - 49\u00d720 = 1000 - 980 = 20 mod 49. Possibly messy; but given previous exact division, likely correct.\n\n---\n\nThe exact integer remain