    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 6070765^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\nWe can write:\n\n\\[\n6070765 = 6,070,765\n\\]\n\nLet's use the identity \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\).\n\nLet \\( a = 6,070,000 \\) and \\( b = 765 \\).\n\n- \\( a^2 = (6,070,000)^2 = (607 \\times 10^4)^2 = 607^2 \\times 10^8 \\).\n  - \\( 607^2 = (600 + 7)^2 = 360000 + 8400 + 49 = 368449 \\).\n  - So \\( a^2 = 368449 \\times 10^8 = 36,844,900,000,000 \\).\n\n- \\( 2ab = 2 \\times 6,070,000 \\times 765 \\).\n  - First, \\( 6,070,000 \\times 765 = 6,070,000 \\times (700 + 60 + 5) \\).\n    - \\( 6,070,000 \\times 700 = 4,249,000,000 \\)\n    - \\( 6,070,000 \\times 60 = 364,200,000 \\)\n    - \\( 6,070,000 \\times 5 = 30,350,000 \\)\n    - Sum: \\( 4,249,000,000 + 364,200,000 = 4,613,200,000 \\), plus \\( 30,350,000 \\) gives \\( 4,643,550,000 \\).\n  - Multiply by 2: \\( 9,287,100,000 \\).\n\n- \\( b^2 = 765^2 = (700 + 65)^2 = 490000 + 2 \\times 700 \\times 65 + 65^2 \\).\n  - \\( 2 \\times 700 \\times 65 = 91,000 \\)\n  - \\( 65^2 = 4225 \\)\n  - Sum: \\( 490,000 + 91,000 = 581,000 \\), plus \\( 4,225 \\) = \\( 585,225 \\).\n\nNow sum:\n\n\\[\n36,844,900,000,000 + 9,287,100,000 = 36,854,187,100,000\n\\]\nAdd \\( 585,225 \\):\n\n\\[\n36,854,187,100,000 + 585,225 = 36,854,187,685,225\n\\]\n\nSo the exact square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36854187685225}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 36854187685225  \nConfidence: 100%"
