585{,}225 \\):  \n\\( 36{,}854{,}187{,}100{,}000 + 585{,}225 = 36{,}854{,}187{,}685{,}225 \\).\n\nSo the final result is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36854187685225}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 36854187685225  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 6070765^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\nWe can write \\( 6070765 = 6,070,765 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Use the identity \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\)**\n\nLet:\n- \\( a = 6,070,000 \\)\n- \\( b = 765 \\)\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\n(6,070,000 + 765)^2\n= 6,070,000^2 + 2 \\times 6,070,000 \\times 765 + 765^2\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Compute each term**\n\nFirst term:\n\\[\n6,070,000^2 = (6.07 \\times 10^6)^2 = 36.8449 \\times 10^{12} = 36,844,900,000,000\n\\]\nLet's check: \\( 6070^2 = 36,844,900 \\), then append 6 zeros (since \\(6,070,000 = 6070 \\times 1000\\)) \u2192 \\(36,844,900,000,000\\). Correct.\n\n---\n\nSecond term:\n\\[\n2 \\times 6,070,000 \\times 765\n\\]\nFirst \\(6,070,000 \\times 765\\):\n- \\(6,070,000 \\times 700 = 4,249,000,000\\)\n- \\(6,070,000 \\times 60 = 364,200,000\\)\n- \\(6,070,000 \\times 5 = 30,350,000\\)\n\nSum: \\(4,249,000,000 + 364,200,000 = 4,613,200,000\\), plus \\(30,350,000\\) = \\(4,643,550,000\\).\n\nMultiply by 2:\n\\[\n2 \\times 4,643,550,000 = 9,287,100,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\nThird term:\n\\[\n765^2 = (700+65)^2 = 490,000 + 2 \\times 700 \\times 65 + 65^2\n\\]\n- \\(2 \\times 700 \\times 65 = 91,000\\)\n- \\(65^2 = 4,225\\)\n\nSum: \\(490,000 + 91,000 = 581,000\\), plus \\(4,225\\) = \\(585,225\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Add them up**\n\n\\[\n36,844,900,000,000 + 9,287,100,000 = 36,854,187,100,000\n\\]\nThen add \\(585,225\\):\n\\[\n36,854,187,100,000 + 585,225 = 36,854,187,685,225\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{36854187685225}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 36854187685225  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 6070765^2 \\).\n\nFirst, note that:\n\n\\( 6070765 = 6,070,765 \\).\n\nWe can split it as \\( 6,070,000 + 765 \\).\n\n- \\( 6,070,000^2 = (6.07 \\times 10^6)^2 = 36.8449 \\times 10^{12} = 36,844,900,000,000 \\).