    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 68281295 \\mod 671 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 671 = 11 \\times 61 \\).\n\nWe can do the division step-by-step.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Estimate quotient**\n\n\\( 671 \\times 100000 = 67,100,000 \\), which is slightly less than 68,281,295.\n\nDifference:  \n\\( 68,281,295 - 67,100,000 = 1,181,295 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Divide the remainder further**\n\n\\( 671 \\times 1000 = 671,000 \\).  \n\\( 1,181,295 - 671,000 = 510,295 \\).\n\nSo far quotient = 101,000.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Continue**\n\n\\( 671 \\times 700 = 469,700 \\).  \n\\( 510,295 - 469,700 = 40,595 \\).\n\nQuotient so far: 101,700.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Continue**\n\n\\( 671 \\times 60 = 40,260 \\).  \n\\( 40,595 - 40,260 = 335 \\).\n\nQuotient so far: 101,760.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Check remainder**\n\n335 is less than 671, so remainder = 335.\n\n---\n\nLet\u2019s verify quickly:  \n\\( 671 \\times 101,760 = 671 \\times (100,000 + 1,760) \\)  \n= \\( 67,100,000 + 671 \\times 1,760 \\).  \n\\( 671 \\times 1,760 = 671 \\times (1,700 + 60) = 1,140,700 + 40,260 = 1,180,960 \\).  \nSum: \\( 67,100,000 + 1,180,960 = 68,280,960 \\).  \nAdd remainder 335: \\( 68,280,960 + 335 = 68,281,295 \\). Correct.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:** 335.\n\nAnswer: 335  \nConfidence: 100%"
