    "raw": "Let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\( 68281295 \\mod 671 \\).\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Check for simplification\nFirst, see if 671 factors nicely.\n\n\\( 671 = 11 \\times 61 \\) (since \\( 11 \\times 61 = 671 \\)).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Use the Chinese Remainder Theorem approach\nWe can find the remainder mod 11 and mod 61, then combine.\n\n---\n\n#### Mod 11:\nUse the alternating sum rule for mod 11:\nNumber: \\( 68281295 \\).\n\nFrom the right:  \nPositions (starting at units = position 1):  \nDigits: 6 8 2 8 1 2 9 5  \nFrom right to left: 5(pos1), 9(pos2), 2(pos3), 1(pos4), 8(pos5), 2(pos6), 8(pos7), 6(pos8).\n\nSum of odd positions: 5 + 2 + 8 + 8 = 23  \nSum of even positions: 9 + 1 + 2 + 6 = 18\n\nDifference = 23 - 18 = 5, which is not a multiple of 11.\n\nSo \\( 68281295 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{11} \\).\n\n---\n\n#### Mod 61:\nWe can do direct division or use modular reduction.\n\nLet\u2019s do stepwise:\n\nFirst, \\( 10^3 = 1000 \\equiv 1000 - 16\\times 61 = 1000 - 976 = 24 \\pmod{61} \\).\n\nMaybe easier: break number into chunks.\n\nNumber = 68,281,295.  \nBut perhaps easier: Let\u2019s do long division mod 61.\n\nStart from left:  \n6 mod 61 = 6  \n6\u00d710+8=68 \u2192 68 mod 61 = 7  \n7\u00d710+2=72 \u2192 72 mod 61 = 11  \n11\u00d710+8=118 \u2192 118 - 61 = 57  \n57\u00d710+1=571 \u2192 571 - 9\u00d761=571-549=22  \n22\u00d710+2=222 \u2192 222 - 3\u00d761=222-183=39  \n39\u00d710+9=399 \u2192 399 - 6\u00d761=399-366=33  \n33\u00d710+5=335 \u2192 335 - 5\u00d761=335-305=30\n\nSo remainder mod 61 = 30.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Solve CRT\nWe have:  \n\\( x \\equiv 5 \\pmod{11} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 30 \\pmod{61} \\)\n\nFrom first: \\( x = 5 + 11k \\).  \nPlug into second: \\( 5 + 11k \\equiv 30 \\pmod{61} \\)  \nSo \\( 11k \\equiv 25 \\pmod{61} \\).\n\nFind inverse of 11 mod 61:  \n61 = 5\u00d711 + 6  \n11 = 1\u00d76 + 5  \n6 = 1\u00d75 + 1  \nBack substitute:  \n1 = 6 - 1\u00d75  \n5 = 11 - 1\u00d76  \nSo 1 = 6 - (11 - 6) = 2\u00d76 - 11  \n6 = 61 - 5\u00d711  \nSo 1 = 2\u00d7(61 - 5\u00d711) - 11 = 2\u00d761 - 10\u00d711 - 11 = 2\u00d761 - 11\u00d711  \n\nThus -11\u00d711 \u2261 1 mod 61, so inverse of 11 is -11 \u2261 50 mod 61.\n\nMultiply: \\( k \\equiv 25 \\times 50 = 1250 \\).  \n1250 mod 61: 61\u00d720=1220, remainder 30. So \\( k \\equiv 30 \\pmod{61} \\).\n\nThus \\( x = 5 + 11\\times 30 = 5 + 330 = 335 \\).\n\nSince 335 < 671, that's the smallest positive solution.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Conclusion\nThe remainder is \\( \\mathbf{335} \\).\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 335  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 68281295 \\) is divided by \\( 671 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Estimate the quotient**\n\nFirst, check how many times 671 goes into 68,281,295.\n\nWe can approximate:  \n\\( 671 \\times 100,000 = 67,100,000 \\).  \n\nSubtract:  \n\\( 68,281,295 - 67,100,000 = 1,181,295 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Further division**\n\nNow, see how many times 671 goes into 1,181,295.\n\n\\( 671 \\times 1000 = 671,000 \\)  \nRemaining: \\( 1,181,295 - 671,000 = 510,295 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: More division**\n\n\\( 671 \\times 700 = 469,700 \\)  \nRemaining: \\( 510,295 - 469,700 = 40,595 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Continue**\n\n\\( 671 \\times 60 = 40,260 \\)  \nRemaining: \\( 40,595 - 40,260 = 335 \\).\n\nSince 335 < 671, we stop.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Total quotient and remainder check**\n\nWe had:\n\n- 100,000 \u00d7 671  \n- 1,000 \u00d7 671  \n- 700 \u00d7 671  \n- 60 \u00d7 671  \n\nTotal multiplier: \\( 100,000 + 1,000 + 700 + 60 = 101,760 \\).\n\nCheck: \\( 671 \\times 101,760 = ? \\)\n\n\\( 671 \\times 100,000 = 67,100,000 \\)  \n\\( 671 \\times 1,760 = 671 \\times 1,700 + 671 \\times 60 = 1,140,700 + 40,260 = 1,180,960 \\)  \nSum: \\( 67,100,000 + 1,180,960 = 68,280,960 \\).\n\nOriginal number: \\( 68,281,295 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 68,281,295 - 68,280,960 = 335 \\).\n\n---\n\nSo remainder = 335.\n\n---\n\n**Final check**: 335 < 671, so correct.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 335  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\( 68281295 \\mod 671 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Estimate division**\n\nFirst, check how many times 671 goes into 68281295.\n\nWe can do long division or use modular reduction.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Use modular arithmetic**\n\nFirst, note \\( 671 = 11 \\times 61 \\), but maybe direct division is simpler.\n\nLet's divide:\n\n- \\( 671 \\times 100000 = 67,100,000 \\).  \n  Subtract from 68,281,295 \u2192 remainder \\( 1,181,295 \\).\n\n- \\( 671 \\times 1000 = 671,000 \\).  \n  \\( 1,181,295 - 671,000 = 510,295 \\).\n\n- \\( 671 \\times 700 = 469,700 \\).  \n  \\( 510,295 - 469,700 = 40,595 \\).\n\n- \\( 671 \\times 60 = 40,260 \\).  \n  \\( 40,595 - 40,260 = 335 \\).\n\nSince 335 < 671, remainder = 335.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Check**\n\n\\( 671 \\times (100000 + 1000 + 700 + 60) = 671 \\times 101760 \\).  \nCompute \\( 671 \\times 101760 \\):\n\n- \\( 671 \\times 100000 = 67,100,000 \\)  \n- \\( 671 \\times 1760 = 671 \\times (1700 + 60) = 1,140,700 + 40,260 = 1,180,960 \\).  \nSum = \\( 67,100,000 + 1,180,960 = 68,280,960 \\).\n\nDifference: \\( 68,281,295 - 68,280,960 = 335\\). \u2705\n\n---\n\n**Final answer**:  \nAnswer: 335  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet\u2019s go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder of \\( 68281295 \\div 671 \\).\n\nFirst, estimate:  \n\\( 671 \\times 100000 = 67,100,000 \\) \u2014 too high.  \nWe want something close to 68,281,295.\n\nTry \\( 671 \\times 100000 \\) is too big, so maybe first find roughly:  \n\\( 671 \\times 100000 = 67,100,000 \\)  \nDifference: \\( 68,281,295 - 67,100,000 = 1,181,295 \\).\n\nNow divide 1,181,295 by 671:  \n\\( 671 \\times 1000 = 671,000 \\), remainder 510,295.  \n\\( 671 \\times 700 = 469,700 \\), remainder 40,595.  \n\\( 671 \\times 60 = 40,260 \\), remainder 335.  \n\\( 671 \\times 0 \\) \u2026 335 < 671, so remainder is 335.\n\nSo total quotient: \\( 100000 + 1000 + 700 + 60 = 101760\\), remainder 335.\n\nLet\u2019s verify quickly:  \n\\( 671 \\times 101760 = 671 \\times (100000 + 1760) \\)  \n\\(= 67,100,000 + 671 \\times 1760\\).  \n\\(671 \\times 1760 = 671 \\times (1700 + 60) = 1,140,700 + 40,260 = 1,180,960\\).  \nAdd: \\(67,100,000 + 1,180,960 = 68,280,960\\).  \nGiven number: 68,281,295; difference = 335. Yes.\n\n**Answer: 335**  \n**Confidence: 100%**\n\nAnswer: 335\nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 68281295 \\mod 671 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 671 = 11 \\times 61 \\).\n\nWe can use the modular approach step-by-step.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Modulo 11**\n\nUsing the alternating sum method for mod 11:\n\nDigits of 68281295: \\(6, 8, 2, 8, 1, 2, 9, 5\\).\n\nAlternating sum:  \n\\((6 - 8 + 2 - 8 + 1 - 2 + 9 - 5)\\)  \n= \\( (6 - 8) = -2; -2 + 2 = 0; 0 - 8 = -8; -8 + 1 = -7; -7 - 2 = -9; -9 + 9 = 0; 0 - 5 = -5\\).\n\nSo remainder mod 11 is \\(-5 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Modulo 61**\n\nFirst, \\(68281295 \\mod 61\\).\n\nLet's reduce step-by-step:\n\n61 \u00d7 1,000,000 = 61,000,000, difference: 68,281,295 \u2212 61,000,000 = 7,281,295.\n\nNow 61 \u00d7 100,000 = 6,100,000, remainder: 7,281,295 \u2212 6,100,000 = 1,181,295.\n\n61 \u00d7 19,000 = 1,159,000, remainder: 1,181,295 \u2212 1,159,000 = 22,295.\n\n61 \u00d7 365 = 22,265, remainder: 22,295 \u2212 22,265 = 30.\n\nSo remainder mod 61 is 30.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Combine via Chinese Remainder Theorem**\n\nWe want \\(x \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\\) and \\(x \\equiv 30 \\pmod{61}\\).\n\nLet \\(x = 30 + 61k\\).  \nWe need \\(30 + 61k \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\n61 mod 11 = 6 (since 55 is multiple of 11, 61 \u2212 55 = 6).  \n30 mod 11 = 8.\n\nSo: \\(8 + 6k \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\\) \u21d2 \\(6k \\equiv -2 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\nFind inverse of 6 mod 11: 6\u00d72=12\u22611, so inverse is 2.\n\nMultiply: \\(k \\equiv 9\u00d72 = 18 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\nSo \\(k = 7 + 11t\\).\n\nThen \\(x = 30 + 61(7 + 11t) = 30 + 427 + 671t = 457 + 671t\\).\n\nSo remainder mod 671 is 457 (since 457 < 671).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Check**\n\n671\u00d710