    "raw": "Let\u2019s do this step-by-step.\n\nWe need the remainder of \\( 26030999 \\div 802 \\).\n\nFirst, approximate:  \n\\( 802 \\times 30000 = 24,060,000 \\), which is less than 26,030,999.\n\nDifference:  \n\\( 26,030,999 - 24,060,000 = 1,970,999 \\).\n\nNow, \\( 802 \\times 2000 = 1,604,000 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 1,970,999 - 1,604,000 = 366,999 \\).\n\nNext, \\( 802 \\times 400 = 320,800 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 366,999 - 320,800 = 46,199 \\).\n\nThen, \\( 802 \\times 50 = 40,100 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 46,199 - 40,100 = 6,099 \\).\n\nFinally, \\( 802 \\times 7 = 5,614 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 6,099 - 5,614 = 485 \\).\n\nSince \\( 485 < 802 \\), that's our remainder.\n\nDouble-check: total quotient = \\(30000 + 2000 + 400 + 50 + 7 = 32457\\).  \nCheck: \\(802 \\times 32457 = 802 \\times (32000 + 457) = 25,664,000 + (802 \\times 457)\\).\n\n\\(802 \\times 457 = 802 \\times 400 + 802 \\times 57 = 320,800 + 45,714 = 366,514\\).  \nSum: \\(25,664,000 + 366,514 = 26,030,514\\).  \nThen 26,030,999 - 26,030,514 = 485. Confirmed.\n\nAnswer: 485  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's do the division step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\( 26030999 \\mod 802 \\).\n\nFirst, let's estimate:\n\n\\( 802 \\times 30000 = 24060000 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 26030999 - 24060000 = 1970999 \\).\n\nNow divide 1,970,999 by 802.\n\n\\( 802 \\times 2000 = 1604000 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 1970999 - 1604000 = 366999 \\).\n\n\\( 802 \\times 400 = 320800 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 366999 - 320800 = 46199 \\).\n\n\\( 802 \\times 50 = 40100 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 46199 - 40100 = 6099 \\).\n\n\\( 802 \\times 7 = 5614 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 6099 - 5614 = 485 \\).\n\n485 is less than 802, so remainder is 485.\n\nCheck: \\( 30000 + 2000 + 400 + 50 + 7 = 32457 \\).  \n\\( 802 \\times 32457 = 802 \\times 32000 + 802 \\times 457 \\).  \n\\( 802 \\times 32000 = 25664000 \\).  \n\\( 802 \\times 457 = 802 \\times 400 + 802 \\times 57 = 320800 + 45714 = 366514 \\).  \nSum: \\( 25664000 + 366514 = 26030514 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 26030999 - 26030514 = 485 \\). \u2705\n\nSo remainder is **485**.\n\nAnswer: 485  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet\u2019s go step-by-step.\n\nWe need the remainder of \\( 26030999 \\div 802 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\( 802 = 2 \\times 401 \\).  \n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Divide by 2:**  \nSince 26030999 is odd, the remainder mod 2 is 1, so we can't directly use Chinese Remainder Theorem in the simplest form without checking mod 401 first.\n\nLet\u2019s do direct division:\n\nEstimate:  \n\\( 802 \\times 30000 = 24,060,000 \\)  \nDifference: \\( 26,030,999 - 24,060,000 = 1,970,999 \\).\n\nNow \\( 802 \\times 2000 = 1,604,000 \\)  \nSubtract: \\( 1,970,999 - 1,604,000 = 366,999 \\).\n\nNow \\( 802 \\times 400 = 320,800 \\)  \nSubtract: \\( 366,999 - 320,800 = 46,199 \\).\n\nNow \\( 802 \\times 50 = 40,100 \\)  \nSubtract: \\( 46,199 - 40,100 = 6,099 \\).\n\nNow \\( 802 \\times 7 = 5,614 \\)  \nSubtract: \\( 6,099 - 5,614 = 485 \\).\n\n485 is less than 802, so remainder is 485.\n\nLet\u2019s verify:  \n\\( 802 \\times 32457 = 802 \\times (30000 + 2000 + 400 + 50 + 7) \\)  \n= 24,060,000 + 1,604,000 + 320,800 + 40,100 + 5,614 = 26,030,514.  \n26,030,999 - 26,030,514 = 485. Correct.\n\n**Final Answer:** 485\n\nAnswer: 485  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 26030999 \\) is divided by \\( 802 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Simplify the division**\n\nFirst, note that \\( 802 = 2 \\times 401 \\).\n\nChecking if 26030999 is odd or even:  \nIt ends with 9, so it's odd. This means the remainder modulo 802 will also be odd.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Compute modulo 2 and modulo 401**\n\nSince 802 = 2 \u00d7 401 and gcd(2, 401) = 1, we can use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n- Mod 2: 26030999 is odd \u2192 remainder mod 2 = 1.\n\n- Mod 401: We need \\( 26030999 \\bmod 401 \\).\n\nFirst, divide 26030999 by 401.\n\n401 \u00d7 60000 = 24,060,000.  \n26030999 \u2212 24060000 = 1,970,999.\n\n401 \u00d7 4000 = 1,604,000.  \n1,970,999 \u2212 1,604,000 = 366,999.\n\n401 \u00d7 900 = 360,900.  \n366,999 \u2212 360,900 = 6,099.\n\n401 \u00d7 15 = 6,015.  \n6,099 \u2212 6,015 = 84.\n\nSo remainder is 84 modulo 401.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Solve CRT**\n\nWe want x \u2261 1 (mod 2), x \u2261 84 (mod 401), with 0 \u2264 x < 802.\n\nSince 84 is even, but mod 2 we need 1, we add 401 (which is odd) to 84:  \n84 + 401 = 485 (odd) \u2014 works for mod 2.\n\nCheck: 485 mod 401 = 84, mod 2 = 1.  \nSo x = 485.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Final check**\n\n485 < 802, so that's the remainder.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 485  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nLet's do the division step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 26030999 \\) is divided by \\( 802 \\).\n\nFirst, note:  \n\\( 802 \\times 100000 = 80,200,000 \\) \u2014 that\u2019s too large. Let's scale down.\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Estimate quotient**  \n\\( 802 \\times 30000 = 24,060,000 \\)  \nDifference: \\( 26,030,999 - 24,060,000 = 1,970,999 \\).\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Continue**  \n\\( 802 \\times 2000 = 1,604,000 \\)  \nRemaining: \\( 1,970,999 - 1,604,000 = 366,999 \\).\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Continue**  \n\\( 802 \\times 400 = 320,800 \\)  \nRemaining: \\( 366,999 - 320,800 = 46,199 \\).\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Continue**  \n\\( 802 \\times 50 = 40,100 \\)  \nRemaining: \\( 46,199 - 40,100 = 6,099 \\).\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Continue**  \n\\( 802 \\times 7 = 5,614 \\)  \nRemaining: \\( 6,099 - 5,614 = 485 \\).\n\nSince 485 < 802, the remainder is \\( 485 \\).\n\n**Final check** \u2014 using modular arithmetic:  \nWe can check \\( 26030999 \\mod 802 \\):\n\nDivide \\( 26030999 \\) by \\( 802 \\):  \n\\( 802 \\times 32457 = 802 \\times (32000 + 457) \\)  \n= \\( 25,664,000 + 802\\times 457 \\)  \n\\( 802 \\times 457 = 802\\times 400 + 802\\times 57 = 320,800 + 45,714 = 366,514 \\)  \nSum: \\( 25,664,000 + 366,514 = 26,030,514 \\)  \nDifference: \\( 26,030,999 - 26,030,514 = 485 \\). \u2713\n\nAnswer: 485  \nConfidence: 100%"
