9.\n\n---\n\nSince 30 < 761, we stop. The remainder is 30.\n\n---\n\n**Final check:**  \nMultiplication: 761 \u00d7 1,429,589 =  \n1,429,589 \u00d7 700 = 1,000,712,300  \n1,429,589 \u00d7 60 = 85,775,340  \n1,429,589 \u00d7 1 = 1,429,589  \nSum: 1,000,712,300 + 85,775,340 = 1,086,487,640 + 1,429,589 = 1,087,917,229.  \nAdd remainder 30 \u2192 1,087,917,259, matches.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 30  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\(1087917259 \\mod 761\\).\n\nFirst, note \\(761\\) is close to \\(760\\). Let's try to reduce the number using modular arithmetic.\n\nBut it might be simpler to do long division or use the fact that 761 is prime (check: not divisible by small primes up to its square root ~27.6; 761 not divisible by 3,5,7,11,13,17,19,23 \u2014 so prime).\n\nWe can use the method:\n\nWe want \\(1087917259 \\div 761\\) remainder.\n\nFirst, approximate:  \n\\(761 \\times 1,000,000 = 761,000,000\\)  \nSubtract: \\(1,087,917,259 - 761,000,000 = 326,917,259\\).\n\nNow \\(761 \\times 400,000 = 304,400,000\\)  \nSubtract: \\(326,917,259 - 304,400,000 = 22,517,259\\).\n\nNext \\(761 \\times 29,000 = 22,069,000\\)  \nSubtract: \\(22,517,259 - 22,069,000 = 448,259\\).\n\nNext \\(761 \\times 500 = 380,500\\)  \nSubtract: \\(448,259 - 380,500 = 67,759\\).\n\nNext \\(761 \\times 80 = 60,880\\)  \nSubtract: \\(67,759 - 60,880 = 6,879\\).\n\nNext \\(761 \\times 9 = 6,849\\)  \nSubtract: \\(6,879 - 6,849 = 30\\).\n\nSo remainder is 30.\n\nLet\u2019s check the multiplier sum:  \n1,000,000 + 400,000 + 29,000 + 500 + 80 + 9 = 1,429,589.\n\nMultiply 761 \u00d7 1,429,589:  \n761 \u00d7 1,429,589 = 1,087,917,229 (let's check: 761\u00d71,400,000=1,065,400,000; 761\u00d729,589=22,517,229; sum=1,087,917,229). Yes.\n\nAdd remainder 30 \u2192 1,087,917,259. Correct.\n\nAnswer: 30\n\nConfidence: 100%\n\nAnswer: 30\nConfidence: 100%\n---\nWe need the remainder of \\(1087917259 \\div 761\\).\n\nLet's do the division step-by-step.\n\nFirst, approximate:  \n\\(761 \\times 1{,}000{,}000 = 761{,}000{,}000\\)  \nDifference: \\(1{,}087{,}917{,}259 - 761{,}000{,}000 = 326{,}917{,}259\\).\n\nNext, \\(761 \\times 400{,}000 = 304{,}400{,}000\\)  \nDifference: \\(326{,}917{,}259 - 304{,}400{,}000 = 22{,}517{,}259\\).\n\nNext, \\(761 \\times 29{,}000 = 22{,}069{,}000\\)  \nDifference: \\(22{,}517{,}259 - 22{,}069{,}000 = 448{,}259\\).\n\nNext, \\(761 \\times 500 = 380{,}500\\)  \nDifference: \\(448{,}259 - 380{,}500 = 67{,}759\\).\n\nNext, \\(761 \\times 80 = 60{,}880\\)  \nDifference: \\(67{,}759 - 60{,}880 = 6{,}879\\).\n\nNext, \\(761 \\times 9 = 6{,}849\\)  \nDifference: \\(6{,}879 - 6{,}849 = 30\\).\n\nSo remainder is \\(30\\).\n\nLet\u2019s double-check by modular arithmetic:\n\nWe can compute \\(1087917259 \\mod 761\\):\n\nBreak 1087917259 into smaller parts mod 761.  \n\nFirst, \\(10^3 = 1000 \\equiv 1000 - 761 = 239 \\pmod{761}\\).  \n\\(10^6 \\equiv 239^2 = 57121\\). Now \\(761 \\times 75 = 57075\\), remainder \\(57121 - 57075 = 46\\).  \nSo \\(10^6 \\equiv 46\\).\n\n\\(10^9 = 10^6 \\times 10^3 \\equiv 46 \\times 239 = 10994\\).  \n\\(761 \\times 14 = 10654\\), remainder \\(10994 - 10654 = 340\\).\n\nNow 1087917259 can be split: \\(1,087,917,259 = 1 \\times 10^9 + 87,917,259\\)? Wait, that\u2019s not the right split.\n\nBetter: \\(1,087,917,259 = 1,087 \\times 10^6 + 917,259\\)? Let\u2019s check: \\(1,087 \\times 10^6 = 1,087,000,000\\), plus 917,259 = 1,087,917,259. Yes.\n\nSo mod 761:  \n\\(1,087 \\mod 761 = 326\\) (since 761\u00d71=761, remainder 326).  \n\\(917,259 \\mod 761\\):  \nFirst 917,259 \u00f7 761: 761\u00d71200=913,200, remainder 4,059. Then 761\u00d75=3,805, remainder 254.\n\nSo \\(917,259 \\equiv 254\\).\n\nAlso \\(10^6 \\equiv 46 \\pmod{761}\\).\n\nThus total mod = \\((326 \\times 46) + 254 \\pmod{761}\\).  \n326\u00d746 = 14,996.  \n14,996 mod 761: 761\u00d719=14,459, remainder 537.  \n537 + 254 = 791.  \n791 mod 761 = 30.\n\nConfirmed remainder is 30.\n\nAnswer: 30  \nConfidence: 100%"
