0 = 227,298.\n\n733 \u00d7 300 = 219,900  \n227,298 \u2212 219,900 = 7,398.\n\n733 \u00d7 10 = 7,330  \n7,398 \u2212 7,330 = 68.\n\nSo total quotient so far: 100,000 + 18,000 + 300 + 10 = 118,310, remainder 68.  \n\nCheck: 733 \u00d7 118,310 = 733 \u00d7 (118,000 + 310) = 733\u00d7118,000 + 733\u00d7310.  \n\n733\u00d7118,000 = 733\u00d7118 \u00d7 1000.  \n733\u00d7118 = 733\u00d7(100+18) = 73,300 + 13,194 = 86,494 \u2192 \u00d71000 = 86,494,000.  \n\n733\u00d7310 = 733\u00d7(300+10) = 219,900 + 7,330 = 227,230.  \n\nSum = 86,494,000 + 227,230 = 86,721,230.  \n\nGiven number: 86,721,298. Difference: 86,721,298 \u2212 86,721,230 = 68. Yes.\n\n---\n\nSo remainder is 68.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\n\nAnswer: 68  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder of \\( 86721298 \\div 733 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Estimate the quotient**  \nFirst, see about how many times 733 goes into 86,721,298.\n\n733 \u00d7 100,000 = 73,300,000  \nRemaining: 86,721,298 \u2212 73,300,000 = 13,421,298.\n\n733 \u00d7 10,000 = 7,330,000  \nRemaining: 13,421,298 \u2212 7,330,000 = 6,091,298.\n\n733 \u00d7 8,000 = 5,864,000  \nRemaining: 6,091,298 \u2212 5,864,000 = 227,298.\n\n733 \u00d7 300 = 219,900  \nRemaining: 227,298 \u2212 219,900 = 7,398.\n\n733 \u00d7 10 = 7,330  \nRemaining: 7,398 \u2212 7,330 = 68.\n\n68 is smaller than 733, so we stop.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Check quotient total**  \nQuotient = 100,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 300 + 10 = 118,310.\n\nCheck: 733 \u00d7 118,310 = 733 \u00d7 (118,000 + 310)  \n733 \u00d7 118,000 = 733 \u00d7 118 \u00d7 1000.  \n733 \u00d7 118 = 733 \u00d7 (100 + 18) = 73,300 + 13,194 = 86,494.  \nTimes 1000 \u2192 86,494,000.\n\n733 \u00d7 310 = 733 \u00d7 (300 + 10) = 219,900 + 7,330 = 227,230.\n\nSum: 86,494,000 + 227,230 = 86,721,230.\n\nOriginal number is 86,721,298, so remainder = 86,721,298 \u2212 86,721,230 = 68.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Conclusion**  \nThe remainder is indeed 68.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 68  \n