ect.\n\n**Answer:** 740\n\nConfidence: 100%\n\nAnswer: 740\nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\( 4805002643 \\mod 741 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Break down the modulus**\n\nFirst, factor \\( 741 \\):\n\n\\[\n741 = 3 \\times 247\n\\]\n\\[\n247 = 13 \\times 19\n\\]\nSo:\n\\[\n741 = 3 \\times 13 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nWe can find the remainder mod 3, mod 13, and mod 19, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Mod 3**\n\nSum of digits of 4805002643:  \n\\(4+8+0+5+0+0+2+6+4+3 = 32\\)  \n32 mod 3 = 2.  \nSo:\n\\[\n4805002643 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Mod 13**\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\(4805002643 \\mod 13\\).\n\nWe can do this by breaking the number or using modular reduction step-by-step.\n\nStart with 0:\n\n- 4 \u2192 4\n- 4\u00d710+8 = 48 \u2192 48 mod 13 = 9 (since 13\u00d73=39, remainder 9)\n- 9\u00d710+0 = 90 \u2192 90 mod 13: 13\u00d76=78, remainder 12\n- 12\u00d710+5 = 125 \u2192 13\u00d79=117, remainder 8\n- 8\u00d710+0 = 80 \u2192 13\u00d76=78, remainder 2\n- 2\u00d710+0 = 20 \u2192 remainder 7\n- 7\u00d710+2 = 72 \u2192 13\u00d75=65, remainder 7\n- 7\u00d710+6 = 76 \u2192 13\u00d75=65, remainder 11\n- 11\u00d710+4 = 114 \u2192 13\u00d78=104, remainder 10\n- 10\u00d710+3 = 103 \u2192 13\u00d77=91, remainder 12\n\nSo remainder mod 13 is 12, i.e., \\(-1\\) mod 13.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Mod 19**\n\nProcess similarly:\n\n- 4 \u2192 4\n- 4\u00d710+8=48 \u2192 48 mod 19 = 10 (19\u00d72=38, remainder 10)\n- 10\u00d710+0=100 \u2192 19\u00d75=95, remainder 5\n- 5\u00d710+5=55 \u2192 19\u00d72=38, remainder 17\n- 17\u00d710+0=170 \u2192 19\u00d78=152, remainder 18\n- 18\u00d710+0=180 \u2192 19\u00d79=171, remainder 9\n- 9\u00d710+2=92 \u2192 19\u00d74=76, remainder 16\n- 16\u00d710+6=166 \u2192 19\u00d78=152, remainder 14\n- 14\u00d710+4=144 \u2192 19\u00d77=133, remainder 11\n- 11\u00d710+3=113 \u2192 19\u00d75=95, remainder 18\n\nSo remainder mod 19 is 18, i.e., \\(-1\\) mod 19.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Combine using CRT**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\[\nx \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 12 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 18 \\pmod{19}\n\\]\n\nNotice \\(12 \\equiv -1\\) mod 13, \\(18 \\equiv -1\\) mod 19.  \nSo \\(x \\equiv -1 \\pmod{13}\\) and \\(\\pmod{19}\\).  \nThus \\(x \\equiv -1 \\pmod{13 \\times 19 = 247}\\).\n\nSo \\(x \\equiv 246 \\pmod{247}\\).\n\nWe also have \\(x \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\\).\n\nLet \\(x = 247k + 246\\).\n\nMod 3: 247 \u2261 1 mod 3, 246 \u2261 0 mod 3 (since 246 = 3\u00d782). So:\n\n\\(x \\equiv k \\pmod{3}\\). We need \\(k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\\).\n\nSmallest positive k = 2.\n\nThen \\(x = 247\u00d72 + 246 = 494 + 246 = 740\\).\n\nCheck: 740 mod 741 = 740.\n\n---\n\n**Step 6 \u2013 Check range**\n\n740 is less than 741, so remainder is 740.\n\n---\n\nFinal answer:\n\nAnswer: 740  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nAlright, let\u2019s go step-by-step.\n\nWe need the remainder when \\( 4805002643 \\) is divided by \\( 741 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Check divisibility rules and simplify modulus**\n\nFirst, factor 741:\n\n\\[\n741 = 3 \\times 247 = 3 \\times 13 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nSince 3, 13, and 19 are pairwise coprime, we can find the remainder modulo each and then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Modulo 3:**\n\nSum of digits of 4805002643:\n\n\\( 4+8+0+5+0+0+2+6+4+3 = 32 \\)\n\n32 mod 3 = 2. So the number mod 3 is 2.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Modulo 13:**\n\nWe can do this carefully.\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\( 4805002643 \\mod 13 \\).\n\nMaybe easier to reduce stepwise using chunks:\n\nFirst, note \\( 10^3 = 1000 \\equiv 1000 - 13 \\times 76 = 1000 - 988 = 12 \\equiv -1 \\mod 13 \\).\n\nSo \\( 10^3 \\equiv -1 \\mod 13 \\), hence \\( 10^6 \\equiv 1 \\mod 13 \\).\n\nGroup digits in threes from the right:\n\n\\( 4,805,002,643 \\) \u2192 groups: \\( 4 \\,|\\, 805 \\,|\\, 002 \\,|\\, 643 \\).\n\nThat\u2019s \\( 4\\times 10^9 + 805\\times 10^6 + 2\\times 10^3 + 643 \\).\n\nMod 13:  \n\\( 10^3 \\equiv -1 \\), \\( 10^6 \\equiv 1 \\), \\( 10^9 \\equiv 10^6 \\times 10^3 \\equiv 1\\times (-1) \\equiv -1 \\).\n\nSo:\n\n- \\( 4\\times 10^9 \\equiv 4\\times (-1) = -4 \\)\n- \\( 805\\times 10^6 \\equiv 805\\times 1 = 805 \\); and \\( 805 \\mod 13\\): 13\u00d761=793, remainder 12, so \u2261 12.\n- \\( 2\\times 10^3 \\equiv 2\\times (-1) = -2 \\)\n- \\( 643 \\mod 13\\): 13\u00d749=637, remainder 6.\n\nSum: \\(-4 + 12 - 2 + 6 = 12\\).\n\n12 mod 13 = 12.  \nSo remainder mod 13 = 12.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Modulo 19:**\n\nUse \\( 10^3 = 1000 \\). 19\u00d752=988, remainder 12, so \\( 10^3 \\equiv 12 \\mod 19 \\).\n\nCheck \\( 10^6 \\equiv 12^2 = 144 \\); 144 - 19\u00d77=144-133=11. So 10^6 \u2261 11 mod 19.\n\nThen \\( 10^9 \\equiv 10^6 \\times 10^3 \\equiv 11\\times 12=132\\); 132-19\u00d76=132-114=18 \u2261 -1 mod 19.\n\nGroups as before: \\( 4 \\,|\\, 805 \\,|\\, 002 \\,|\\, 643 \\).\n\nSo mod 19:\n\n- First term: \\( 4\\times 10^9 \\equiv 4\\times (-1) = -4 \\)\n- Second: \\( 805\\times 10^6 \\equiv 805\\times 11 \\). First 805 mod 19: 19\u00d742=798, remainder 7, so 7\u00d711=77; 77-19\u00d74=77-76=1.\n- Third: \\( 2\\times 10^3 \\equiv 2\\times 12=24 \\equiv 5 \\) (since 24-19=5)\n- Fourth: 643 mod 19: 19\u00d733=627, remainder 16.\n\nSum: \\(-4 + 1 + 5 + 16 = 18\\).\n\n18 mod 19 = 18.\n\nSo remainder mod 19 = 18.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 CRT**\n\nWe have:\n\n- \\( x \\equiv 2 \\mod 3 \\)\n- \\( x \\equiv 12 \\mod 13 \\)\n- \\( x \\equiv 18 \\mod 19 \\)\n\nFrom mod 13 and 19: x \u2261 12 mod 13, x \u2261 18 mod 19.\n\nNote 18 \u2261 -1 mod 19, 12 \u2261 -1 mod 13.\n\nSo x \u2261 -1 mod 13 and mod 19 \u21d2 x \u2261 -1 mod (13\u00d719=247).  \nThus x \u2261 246 mod 247.\n\n---\n\nNow combine with mod 3: 246 mod 3 = 0 (since 2+4+6=12 divisible by 3). So x \u2261 0 mod 3.\n\nWe want x \u2261 246 mod 247, x \u2261 0 mod 3.\n\nNumbers \u2261 246 mod 247: 246, 493, 740, 987, ...\n\nCheck mod 3:\n\n- 246 \u2261 0 mod 3 \u2705\n\nSo smallest positive is 246.\n\n---\n\nTherefore remainder is 246.\n\n---\n\n**Step 6 \u2013 Final check**\n\n741\u00d76484 =? Let's check:  \n741\u00d76000=4,446,000  \n741\u00d7484=741\u00d7500 - 741\u00d716 = 370,500 - 11,856 = 358,644  \nSum=4,804,644. Wait, need exact: 4805002643 - 246 = 4805002397. Divide by 741?\n\nCheck 741\u00d76484484? That\u2019s too big. Better check 741\u00d76484484? Let's match digits: maybe 4805002397 / 741.\n\nInstead verify mod 3,13,19 match: earlier we had 246 mod 3=0? Wait, hold on: 246 mod 3=0, but original number mod 3=2. That's a mismatch! I must have made a mistake.\n\n---\n\n**Step 7 \u2013 Catch error**\n\nIndeed, original number mod 3 was 2, not 0. So my CRT assumption x \u2261 -1 mod 247 gave 246 \u2261 0 mod 3, which is wrong. So I need to adjust.\n\nWe want x \u2261 246 mod 247 and x \u2261 2 mod 3.\n\nCheck 246 mod 3=0, not 2. So add 247: 246+247=493, mod 3: 4+9+3=16\u21921 mod 3, not 2. Add again: 740, sum digits=11\u21922 mod 3 \u2705.\n\nSo x=740 works.\n\n---\n\n**Step 8 \u2013 Verify**\n\n740 < 741, so remainder 740? Let's quick check mod 13: 740 mod 13: 13\u00d756=728, remainder 12 \u2705. Mod 19: 19\u00d738=722, remainder 18 \u2705. Mod 3: 740 sum=11\u21922 \u2705.\n\nYes, matches all.\n\n---\n\n**Step 9 \u2013 Conclusion**\n\nAnswer: 740.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 740  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nLet's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 4805002643 \\) is divided by \\( 741 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Break down the modulus**  \n\\( 741 = 3 \\times 247 \\)  \nand \\( 247 = 13 \\times 19 \\), so  \n\\( 741 = 3 \\times 13 \\times 19 \\).\n\nWe could compute the remainder mod 741 directly using division.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Direct division approach**\n\nCompute \\( 4805002643 \\div 741 \\):\n\nFirst, estimate:  \n\\( 741 \\times 6,000,000 = 4,446,000,000 \\) (too small compared to 4.8 billion).  \nLet's check how many times 741 fits into 4,805,002,643.\n\n741 \u00d7 6,500,000 = 4,816,500,000 (slightly too large).  \nDifference: 4,816,500,000 \u2212 4,805,002,643 = 11,497,357 too big, so reduce quotient.\n\nTry 6,480,000:  \n741 \u00d7 6,480,000 = 741 \u00d7 (6,000,000 + 480,000)  \n= 4,446,000,000 + 355,680,000 = 4,801,680,000.\n\nSubtract: 4,805,002,643 \u2212 4,801,680,000 = 3,322,643.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Continue dividing the remainder**\n\nNow, 3,322,643 \u00f7 741:\n\n741 \u00d7 4,000 = 2,964,000.  \nRemainder: 3,322,643 \u2212 2,964,000 = 358,643.\n\n741 \u00d7 400 = 296,400.  \nRemainder: 358,643 \u2212 296,400 = 62,243.\n\n741 \u00d7 80 = 59,280.  \nRemainder: 62,243 \u2212 59,280 = 2,963.\n\n741 \u00d7 3 = 2,223.  \nRemainder: 2,963 \u2212 2,223 = 740.\n\n740 < 741, so we stop.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Combine the quotients and remainder**\n\nQuotient total = 6,480,000 + 4,000 + 400 + 80 + 3 = 6,484,483.  \nRemainder = 740.\n\nCheck: 741 \u00d7 6,484,483 = ?  \n741 \u00d7 6,484,483 = (741 \u00d7 6,480,000) + (741 \u00d7 4,483)  \n= 4,801,680,000 + (741 \u00d7 4,483).  \n741 \u00d7 4,483: 741 \u00d7 4,000 = 2,964,000; 741 \u00d7 483 = 741 \u00d7 400 + 741 \u00d7 80 + 741 \u00d7 3 = 296,400 + 59,280 + 2,223 = 357,903.  \nSum: 2,964,000 + 357,903 = 3,321,903.\n\nAdd: 4,801,680,000 + 3,321,903 = 4,805,001,903.  \nAdd remainder 740 \u2192 4,805,002,643. Correct.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Final answer**\n\nThe remainder is \\( 740 \\).\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 740  \nConfidence: 100%"
