nSo the answer is \\( 30308251015849 \\).\n\nAnswer: 30308251015849  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 5505293^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\nWe can use:\n\n\\[\n(5,505,293)^2\n\\]\n\nLet \\( a = 5,500,000 \\) and \\( b = 5,293 \\).\n\nThen:\n\n\\[\n5505293^2 = (5,500,000 + 5,293)^2\n\\]\n\nUsing the binomial expansion:\n\n\\[\n= 5,500,000^2 + 2 \\times 5,500,000 \\times 5,293 + 5,293^2\n\\]\n\nFirst term:\n\n\\( 5,500,000^2 = (55 \\times 10^5)^2 = 3025 \\times 10^{10} = 30,250,000,000,000 \\)\n\nSecond term:\n\n\\( 2 \\times 5,500,000 \\times 5,293 = 11,000,000 \\times 5,293 = 58,223,000,000 \\)\n\nThird term:\n\n\\( 5,293^2 = (5,300 - 7)^2 = 28,090,000 - 74,200 + 49 \\) wait, let's compute carefully:\n\n\\( 5,293^2 = (5,000 + 293)^2 = 25,000,000 + 2 \\times 5,000 \\times 293 + 293^2 \\)\n\n\\( = 25,000,000 + 2,930,000 + 85,849 \\)\n\n\\( = 27,930,000 + 85,849 = 28,015,849 \\).\n\nNow sum:\n\nFirst term: \\( 30,250,000,000,000 \\)  \nSecond term: \\( 58,223,000,000 \\) \u2192 sum = \\( 30,308,223,000,000 \\)  \nThird term: \\( 28,015,849 \\) \u2192 sum = \\( 30,308,251,015,849 \\).\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\n5505293^2 = 30,308,251,015,849\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 30308251015849  \nConfidence: 100%"
