    "raw": "Let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 22034628 \\) is divided by \\( 670 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Break down the divisor**  \n\\( 670 = 67 \\times 10 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder mod 67 and mod 10, then combine.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 10**  \nThe last digit of \\( 22034628 \\) is 8, so:\n\n\\[\n22034628 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{10}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Mod 67**  \nWe can do this by long division or modular reduction.\n\nFirst, note \\( 67 \\times 328,000 = 21,976,000 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 22,034,628 - 21,976,000 = 58,628 \\).\n\nNow \\( 67 \\times 875 = 58,625 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 58,628 - 58,625 = 3 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 67 is 3.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Combine using Chinese Remainder Theorem**  \nWe need \\( x \\equiv 3 \\pmod{67} \\) and \\( x \\equiv 8 \\pmod{10} \\).\n\nLet \\( x = 3 + 67k \\).  \nWe want \\( 3 + 67k \\equiv 8 \\pmod{10} \\).  \n\\( 67 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{10} \\), so:\n\n\\( 3 + 7k \\equiv 8 \\pmod{10} \\)  \n\\( 7k \\equiv 5 \\pmod{10} \\).\n\nThe inverse of 7 mod 10 is 3 (since \\( 7\\times 3 = 21 \\equiv 1 \\)).  \nMultiply both sides by 3:  \n\\( k \\equiv 15 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{10} \\).\n\nSo \\( k = 5 \\) works (smallest nonnegative).\n\nThen \\( x = 3 + 67\\times 5 = 3 + 335 = 338 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Check**  \n338 < 670, so remainder is 338.\n\nCheck mod 67: \\( 338 - 335 = 3 \\) \u2713  \nCheck mod 10: last digit 8 \u2713\n\n---\n\n**Final answer**:\n\nAnswer: 338  \nConfidence: 100%"
