    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 22034628 \\mod 670 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\( 670 = 67 \\times 10 \\).  \nA quicker way is to directly divide.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Reduce modulo 670**\n\nWe can do:\n\n\\( 670 \\times 32887 = ? \\)  \nLet\u2019s instead do modular reduction directly.\n\nWe can break it:  \n\\( 22034628 \\div 670 \\).\n\n670 \u00d7 30000 = 20,100,000  \nRemainder: 22034628 \u2212 20100000 = 1,934,628.\n\n670 \u00d7 2,000 = 1,340,000 \u2192 remainder: 1,934,628 \u2212 1,340,000 = 594,628.\n\n670 \u00d7 800 = 536,000 \u2192 remainder: 594,628 \u2212 536,000 = 58,628.\n\n670 \u00d7 80 = 53,600 \u2192 remainder: 58,628 \u2212 53,600 = 5,028.\n\n670 \u00d7 7 = 4,690 \u2192 remainder: 5,028 \u2212 4,690 = 338.\n\n338 is less than 670, so remainder is 338.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Check via modular arithmetic**\n\nMod 67:  \nFirst reduce 22034628 mod 67:  \n67 \u00d7 328,875 = 22,034,625 \u2192 remainder 3. So \u2261 3 mod 67.\n\nMod 10: number ends with 8, so \u2261 8 mod 10.\n\nWe want a number \u2261 3 mod 67 and \u2261 8 mod 10, less than 670.\n\nLet x = 3 + 67k.  \nCheck mod 10: 3 + 67k \u2261 3 + 7k \u2261 8 mod 10 \u2192 7k \u2261 5 mod 10.  \n7 inverse mod 10 is 3 (since 7\u00d73=21\u22611), so k \u2261 15 \u2261 5 mod 10.\n\nSmallest k=5 \u2192 x = 3 + 335 = 338. Works.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Conclusion**\n\nRemainder is 338.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 338  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute step by step.\n\nWe want \\( 22034628 \\mod 670 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\( 670 = 67 \\times 10 \\). But since 22034628 is divisible by 2 (ends in 8) and by 5? No, it doesn't end in 0 or 5, so it's not divisible by 5. But 670 = 2 \u00d7 5 \u00d7 67, so easiest might be directly dividing.\n\nLet's do modular reduction:\n\nFirst, 670 \u00d7 30000 = 20,100,000.  \nSubtract: 22,034,628 \u2212 20,100,000 = 1,934,628.\n\nNow 670 \u00d7 2000 = 1,340,000.  \nSubtract: 1,934,628 \u2212 1,340,000 = 594,628.\n\n670 \u00d7 800 = 536,000.  \nSubtract: 594,628 \u2212 536,000 = 58,628.\n\n670 \u00d7 80 = 53,600.  \nSubtract: 58,628 \u2212 53,600 = 5,028.\n\n670 \u00d7 7 = 4,690.  \nSubtract: 5,028 \u2212 4,690 = 338.\n\nSince 338 < 670, remainder is 338.\n\nLet me check quickly: 30,000 + 2,000 + 800 + 80 + 7 = 32,887.  \n670 \u00d7 32,887 = ?\n\n670 \u00d7 32,000 = 21,440,000  \n670 \u00d7 887 = 670 \u00d7 800 = 536,000; 670 \u00d7 87 = 58,290; sum = 594,290.  \nTotal = 21,440,000 + 594,290 = 22,034,290.  \n22,034,628 \u2212 22,034,290 = 338. Yes.\n\nAnswer: 338  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nFirst, I\u2019ll compute \\( 22034628 \\mod 670 \\).\n\nWe can break this into steps:\n\n1. **Divide 22034628 by 670**  \n   First, note \\( 670 = 67 \\times 10 \\).  \n   Let's find the remainder directly.\n\n2. **Use modular reduction:**\n   - \\( 22034628 \\div 670 \\):  \n     \\( 670 \\times 32887 = 670 \\times (33000 - 113) = 22110000 - 75710 = 22034290\\).  \n     Subtract: \\( 22034628 - 22034290 = 338 \\).\n\n3. Since 338 < 670, remainder is 338.\n\nLet me double-check:\n\n- \\(670 \\times 32887\\):\n  - \\(670 \\times 32800 = 21,976,000\\)  \n  - \\(670 \\times 87 = 58,290\\)  \n  - Sum = \\(21,976,000 + 58,290 = 22,034,290\\).  \n- Difference: \\(22,034,628 - 22,034,290 = 338\\). Correct.\n\nSo remainder = 338.\n\nAnswer: 338  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet\u2019s proceed step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 22034628 \\) is divided by \\( 670 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Break down 670**  \n\\( 670 = 67 \\times 10 \\).\n\nWe could also compute directly: \\( 22034628 \\mod 670 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Estimate the quotient**  \n\\( 670 \\times 30000 = 20,100,000 \\), which is a bit less than \\( 22,034,628 \\).  \nDifference: \\( 22,034,628 - 20,100,000 = 1,934,628 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Continue division**  \n\\( 670 \\times 2000 = 1,340,000 \\), difference: \\( 1,934,628 - 1,340,000 = 594,628 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 More division**  \n\\( 670 \\times 800 = 536,000 \\), difference: \\( 594,628 - 536,000 = 58,628 \\).