n67 \u2261 7 mod 10, so \\(3 + 7k \\equiv 8 \\pmod{10} \\Rightarrow 7k \\equiv 5 \\pmod{10}\\).  \n7 inverse mod 10 is 3 (since 7\u00d73=21\u22611), so \\(k \u2261 15 \u2261 5 \\pmod{10}\\). Smallest k=5.  \n\nThen x = 3 + 67\u00d75 = 3 + 335 = 338. Check: 338 mod 10 = 8, mod 67 = 3. Good.\n\n**Step 4: Verify**  \n670 \u00d7 32,000 = 21,440,000 \u2192 difference = 594,628  \n670 \u00d7 887 = 594,290 \u2192 difference = 338. Yes.\n\nSo remainder is 338.\n\nAnswer: 338  \nConfidence: 95%"
