    "raw": "Let's compute step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\( 8631208977 \\mod 524 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\( 524 = 4 \\times 131 \\).  \nWe can compute mod 4 and mod 131, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Mod 4**  \nThe last two digits of 8631208977 are 77.  \n77 mod 4 = 1.  \nSo the number \u2261 1 (mod 4).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 131**  \nWe can reduce 8631208977 mod 131.\n\nFirst, 131 \u00d7 65,000,000 = 8,515,000,000.  \nDifference: 8,631,208,977 \u2212 8,515,000,000 = 116,208,977.\n\nNow reduce 116,208,977 mod 131.\n\n131 \u00d7 887,000 = 116,197,000.  \nDifference: 116,208,977 \u2212 116,197,000 = 11,977.\n\nNow 11,977 mod 131:  \n131 \u00d7 91 = 11,921.  \nDifference: 11,977 \u2212 11,921 = 56.\n\nSo the number \u2261 56 (mod 131).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Solve system**  \nWe have:  \nx \u2261 1 (mod 4)  \nx \u2261 56 (mod 131)\n\nFrom x \u2261 56 (mod 131), x = 56 + 131k.\n\nCheck mod 4: 56 \u2261 0 (mod 4), 131 \u2261 3 (mod 4).  \nSo 56 + 131k \u2261 0 + 3k \u2261 1 (mod 4).  \nThus 3k \u2261 1 (mod 4).  \n3 inverse mod 4 is 3 (since 3\u00d73=9\u22611).  \nSo k \u2261 3 (mod 4).\n\nSmallest k = 3: x = 56 + 131\u00d73 = 56 + 393 = 449.\n\nCheck: 449 mod 4 = 1, 449 mod 131 = 56. Good.\n\nSince 449 < 524, that's the remainder.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Verify**  \n524 \u00d7 16,471,000 = 8,630,804,000.  \nDifference: 8,631,208,977 \u2212 8,630,804,000 = 404,977.  \n404,977 \u00f7 524 = 772 remainder?  \n524 \u00d7 772 = 404,528.  \n404,977 \u2212 404,528 = 449. Yes.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 449  \nConfidence: 100%"
