    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 23617158 \\mod 900 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 900 = 9 \\times 100 \\), and since 9 and 100 are coprime, we can find the remainder modulo 9 and modulo 100, then combine.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Modulo 100**\n\nThe last two digits of 23617158 are 58, so:\n\n\\[\n23617158 \\equiv 58 \\pmod{100}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Modulo 9**\n\nSum of digits of 23617158:\n\n\\( 2+3+6+1+7+1+5+8 = 33 \\)\n\n\\( 33 \\mod 9 = 6 \\), so:\n\n\\[\n23617158 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{9}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Solve system**\n\nWe need \\( x \\equiv 58 \\pmod{100} \\) and \\( x \\equiv 6 \\pmod{9} \\).\n\nLet \\( x = 58 + 100k \\).\n\nModulo 9:\n\n\\( 58 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{9} \\) (since 54 is multiple of 9, remainder 4).\n\n\\( 100 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{9} \\).\n\nSo \\( 4 + k \\equiv 6 \\pmod{9} \\) \u2192 \\( k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{9} \\).\n\nSmallest \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\( x = 58 + 200 = 258 \\).\n\nCheck: \\( 258 \\mod 9 = 6 \\) (since 252 is multiple of 9, remainder 6), and mod 100 is 58. Good.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Verify range**\n\n258 is between 0 and 899, so it's the remainder.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 258  \nConfidence: 100%"
