    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 6710873^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\nWe can write:\n\n\\[\n6710873 = 6{,}710{,}873\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\).\n\nLet\u2019s take \\(a = 6{,}700{,}000\\) and \\(b = 10{,}873\\).\n\n- \\(a^2 = (6.7 \\times 10^6)^2 = 44{,}890{,}000{,}000{,}000\\)  \n  Actually, more precisely:  \n  \\(6{,}700{,}000^2 = (67 \\times 10^5)^2 = 4489 \\times 10^{10} = 44{,}890{,}000{,}000{,}000\\).\n\n- \\(2ab = 2 \\times 6{,}700{,}000 \\times 10{,}873\\)  \n  First: \\(6{,}700{,}000 \\times 10{,}873 = 67 \\times 10^5 \\times 10{,}873\\)  \n  \\(67 \\times 10{,}873 = 728{,}491\\)  \n  Multiply by \\(10^5\\): \\(72{,}849{,}100{,}000\\)  \n  Double it: \\(145{,}698{,}200{,}000\\).\n\n- \\(b^2 = 10{,}873^2\\)  \n  \\(10{,}873^2 = (10{,}000 + 873)^2 = 100{,}000{,}000 + 2 \\times 10{,}000 \\times 873 + 873^2\\)  \n  \\(= 100{,}000{,}000 + 17{,}460{,}000 + 762{,}129\\)  \n  \\(= 118{,}222{,}129\\).\n\nNow sum:\n\n\\[\n44{,}890{,}000{,}000{,}000 + 145{,}698{,}200{,}000 = 45{,}035{,}698{,}200{,}000\n\\]\nAdd \\(118{,}222{,}129\\):\n\n\\[\n45{,}035{,}816{,}422{,}129\n\\]\n\nSo the exact square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45035816422129}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 45035816422129  \nConfidence: 100%"
