    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's compute \\( 6710873^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\n---\n\nWe can use the identity:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nLet\u2019s write \\( 6710873 \\) as \\( 6{,}710{,}000 + 873 \\).\n\nSo:\n\n- \\( a = 6{,}710{,}000 \\)\n- \\( b = 873 \\)\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Compute \\( a^2 \\)**\n\n\\( 6{,}710{,}000^2 = (671 \\times 10^4)^2 = 671^2 \\times 10^8 \\).\n\nFirst, \\( 671^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n671^2 = (670 + 1)^2 = 670^2 + 2 \\cdot 670 \\cdot 1 + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n670^2 = 448{,}900\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 670 = 1{,}340\n\\]\nSo:\n\\[\n671^2 = 448{,}900 + 1{,}340 + 1 = 450{,}241\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n6{,}710{,}000^2 = 450{,}241 \\times 10^8 = 45{,}024{,}100{,}000{,}000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Compute \\( 2ab \\)**\n\n\\( 2ab = 2 \\times 6{,}710{,}000 \\times 873 \\).\n\nFirst, \\( 6{,}710{,}000 \\times 873 \\):\n\nBreak 873 into \\( 800 + 70 + 3 \\):\n\n- \\( 6{,}710{,}000 \\times 800 = 5{,}368{,}000{,}000 \\)\n- \\( 6{,}710{,}000 \\times 70 = 469{,}700{,}000 \\)\n- \\( 6{,}710{,}000 \\times 3 = 20{,}130{,}000 \\)\n\nSum:  \n\\( 5{,}368{,}000{,}000 + 469{,}700{,}000 = 5{,}837{,}700{,}000 \\)  \nPlus \\( 20{,}130{,}000 \\) gives \\( 5{,}857{,}830{,}000 \\).\n\nNow multiply by 2:\n\n\\[\n2ab = 11{,}715{,}660{,}000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Compute \\( b^2 \\)**\n\n\\( 873^2 = (870 + 3)^2 = 870^2 + 2 \\cdot 870 \\cdot 3 + 9 \\).\n\n- \\( 870^2 = 756{,}900 \\)\n- \\( 2 \\cdot 870 \\cdot 3 = 5{,}220 \\)\n- Plus 9.\n\nSum: \\( 756{,}900 + 5{,}220 = 762{,}120 \\), plus 9 = \\( 762{,}129 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Add them up**\n\nWe have:\n\n- \\( a^2 = 45{,}024{,}100{,}000{,}000 \\)\n- \\( 2ab = 11{,}715{,}660{,}000 \\)\n- \\( b^2 = 762{,}129 \\)\n\nFirst add \\( a^2 + 2ab \\):\n\n\\[\n45{,}024{,}100{,}000{,}000 + 11{,}715{,}660{,}000 = 45{,}035{,}815{,}660{,}000\n\\]\n\nNow add \\( b^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n45{,}035{,}815{,}660{,}000 + 762{,}129 = 45{,}035{,}816{,}422{,}129\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45035816422129}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 45035816422129"
