    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 73087744 \\mod 245 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\(245 = 5 \\times 49 = 5 \\times 7^2\\).\n\nWe can find the remainder using modular arithmetic.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Mod 5**\n\nThe last digit is 4, so:\n\n\\[\n73087744 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 49**\n\nWe can reduce the number mod 49.\n\nFirst, \\( 73087744 \\div 49 \\):\n\nLet\u2019s do it stepwise.\n\n49 \u00d7 1,491,586 = ?\n\nBetter: Let's use the fact that \\(100 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{49}\\) since 100 - 98 = 2.\n\nWrite 73087744 in chunks:\n\n73,087,744 = 73 \u00d7 1,000,000 + 87,744? That\u2019s messy. Let's do mod 49 directly.\n\n---\n\nWe can use:\n\n\\(10^2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{49}\\)  \n\\(10^4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{49}\\)  \n\\(10^8 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{49}\\)  \nBut maybe easier: break number into base 100 chunks.\n\nNumber: 73,087,744 \u2192 chunks: 73 | 08 | 77 | 44 (base 100).\n\nWe know \\(100 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{49}\\).\n\nSo value mod 49 = \\(73 \\times 2^3 + 8 \\times 2^2 + 77 \\times 2 + 44\\) mod 49.\n\nCompute:\n\n- \\(2^3 = 8\\), so \\(73 \\times 8 = 584\\).  \n584 mod 49: 49\u00d711=539, remainder 45.\n\n- \\(8 \\times 4 = 32\\).\n\n- \\(77 \\times 2 = 154\\), mod 49: 49\u00d73=147, remainder 7.\n\n- Last chunk: 44.\n\nSum: 45 + 32 = 77 \u2192 77 + 7 = 84 \u2192 84 + 44 = 128.\n\n128 mod 49: 49\u00d72=98, remainder 30.\n\nSo remainder mod 49 is 30.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Combine via CRT**\n\nWe need \\(x \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}\\) and \\(x \\equiv 30 \\pmod{49}\\).\n\nLet \\(x = 30 + 49k\\). Mod 5: 30 \u2261 0, 49 \u2261 4 mod 5.\n\nSo \\(0 + 4k \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\) \u2192 \\(4k \\equiv 4\\) \u2192 \\(k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\\).\n\nSmallest k=1 \u2192 x = 30 + 49 = 79.\n\nCheck: 79 mod 5 = 4, mod 49 = 30. Good.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Check if less than 245** \u2014 yes, 79 < 245.\n\nSo remainder is 79.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 79  \nConfidence: 95%"
