    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 39968745 \\mod 715 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 715 = 5 \\times 11 \\times 13 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder modulo 715 by using the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Modulo 5**\n\nThe last digit is 5, so:\n\n\\[\n39968745 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Modulo 11**\n\nFor mod 11, use the alternating sum of digits:\n\nDigits: \\(3, 9, 9, 6, 8, 7, 4, 5\\) (from left to right).\n\nAlternating sum (starting with + for the first digit):\n\n\\[\n3 - 9 + 9 - 6 + 8 - 7 + 4 - 5\n\\]\nCompute step by step:\n\n\\(3 - 9 = -6\\)  \n\\(-6 + 9 = 3\\)  \n\\(3 - 6 = -3\\)  \n\\(-3 + 8 = 5\\)  \n\\(5 - 7 = -2\\)  \n\\(-2 + 4 = 2\\)  \n\\(2 - 5 = -3\\)\n\nSo sum = \\(-3\\).  \nMod 11: \\(-3 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\nThus remainder mod 11 is 8.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Modulo 13**\n\nWe can do direct division or use modular reduction.\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\(39968745 \\mod 13\\).\n\nFirst, \\(13 \\times 3074518 = 39968734\\), remainder \\(11\\). Let\u2019s check:\n\n\\(13 \\times 3,074,518\\):\n\n\\(3,074,518 \\times 10 = 30,745,180\\)  \n\\(3,074,518 \\times 3 = 9,223,554\\)  \nSum = \\(39,968,734\\).\n\nSubtract from 39,968,745: remainder = 11.\n\nSo mod 13 remainder is 11.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Solve system**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\[\nx \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\n\\]\n\nFirst combine mod 5 and mod 11:\n\nFrom \\(x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}\\), \\(x = 5k\\).\n\n\\(5k \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\\).  \nInverse of 5 mod 11 is 9 (since \\(5\\times 9=45\\equiv 1\\)).\n\nSo \\(k \\equiv 8\\times 9 = 72 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\nThus \\(k = 6 + 11t\\), so \\(x = 5(6+11t) = 30 + 55t\\).\n\nNow \\(x \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\\):\n\n\\(30 + 55t \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\\).\n\n30 mod 13 = 4, 55 mod 13 = 3 (since 52 is multiple of 13, remainder 3).\n\nSo \\(4 + 3t \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\\)  \n\\(\\Rightarrow 3t \\equiv 7 \\pmod{13}\\).\n\nInverse of 3 mod 13 is 9 (since \\(3\\times 9=27\\equiv 1\\)).\n\nSo \\(t \\equiv 7\\times 9 = 63 \\equiv 11 \\pmod{13}\\).\n\nThus \\(t = 11 + 13m\\).\n\nThen \\(x = 30 + 55(11 + 13m) = 30 + 605 + 715m = 635 + 715m\\).\n\nSo remainder mod 715 is 635.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Check**\n\n635 mod 5 = 0 \u2705  \n635 mod 11: 11\u00d757=627, remainder 8 \u2705  \n635 mod 13: 13\u00d748=624, remainder 11 \u2705\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\nAnswer: 635  \nConfidence: 100%"
