 \\( 9{,}250{,}000 \\times 4{,}204 = 9{,}250{,}000 \\times 4{,}000 + 9{,}250{,}000 \\times 204 \\)\n\n- \\( 9{,}250{,}000 \\times 4{,}000 = 37{,}000{,}000{,}000 \\)\n- \\( 9{,}250{,}000 \\times 204 = 9{,}250{,}000 \\times 200 + 9{,}250{,}000 \\times 4 = 1{,}850{,}000{,}000 + 37{,}000{,}000 = 1{,}887{,}000{,}000 \\)\n\nSum: \\( 37{,}000{,}000{,}000 + 1{,}887{,}000{,}000 = 38{,}887{,}000{,}000 \\)\n\nMultiply by 2: \\( 77{,}774{,}000{,}000 \\)\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Compute \\(B^2\\)**\n\n\\( 4{,}204^2 = (4{,}200 + 4)^2 = 17{,}640{,}000 + 2 \\cdot 4{,}200 \\cdot 4 + 16 \\)\n\n- \\( 4{,}200^2 = 17{,}640{,}000 \\)\n- \\( 2 \\cdot 4{,}200 \\cdot 4 = 33{,}600 \\)\n- Add 16: total \\( 17{,}640{,}000 + 33{,}600 + 16 = 17{,}673{,}616 \\)\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Add them up**\n\n\\( A^2 = 85{,}562{,}500{,}000{,}000 \\)  \n\\( 2AB = 77{,}774{,}000{,}000 \\)  \n\\( B^2 = 17{,}673{,}616 \\)\n\nFirst sum \\( A^2 + 2AB = 85{,}640{,}274{,}000{,}000 \\)\n\nAdd \\( B^2 \\): \\( 85{,}640{,}274{,}000{,}000 + 17{,}673{,}616 = 85{,}640{,}291{,}673{,}616 \\)\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{85640291673616}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 85640291673616  \nConfidence: 97%\n---\nAlright, let's compute \\( 9254204^2 \\) step by step.\n\nWe can use the identity:\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nLet \\( a = 9,254,000 \\) and \\( b = 204 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Compute \\( a^2 \\)**\n\\[\n9,254,000^2 = (9254^2) \\times 10^6\n\\]\nFirst, \\( 9254^2 \\):\n\\[\n9254^2 = (9000 + 254)^2 = 81,000,000 + 2 \\times 9000 \\times 254 + 254^2\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\times 9000 \\times 254 = 18,000 \\times 254 = 4,572,000\n\\]\n\\[\n254^2 = 64,516\n\\]\nSum:\n\\[\n81,000,000 + 4,572,000 = 85,572,000\n\\]\n\\[\n85,572,000 + 64,516 = 85,636,516\n\\]\nThus \\( 9254^2 = 85,636,516 \\).  \nSo \\( 9,254,000^2 = 85,636,516 \\times 10^6 = 85,636,516,000,000 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Compute \\( 2ab \\)**\n\\[\n2ab = 2 \\times 9,254,000 \\times 204\n\\]\nFirst \\( 9,254,000 \\times 204 = 9,254,000 \\times (200 + 4) = 1,850,800,000 + 37,016,000 = 1,887,816,000 \\).  \nDouble it:\n\\[\n2ab = 3,775,632,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Compute \\( b^2 \\)**\n\\[\n204^2 = 41,616\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Add them together**\n\\[\n85,636,516,000,000 + 3,775,632,000 = 85,640,291,632,000\n\\]\nAdd \\( 41,616 \\):\n\\[\n85,640,291,632,000 + 41,616 = 85,640,291,673,616\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{85640291673616}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 85640291673616  \nConfidence: 100%"
