    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 4457185027 \\mod 257 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 257 \\) is a prime number (it's a Fermat prime, \\( 2^8 + 1 \\)).\n\nWe can do the division step-by-step.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Break the number into manageable parts.**\n\nWe can use modular reduction directly:\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\( 4457185027 \\mod 257 \\).\n\nWe can do this by long division or by splitting.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Use modular arithmetic with chunks.**\n\nLet\u2019s take the number in chunks of 3 digits from the right:\n\n\\( 4457185027 = 4,457,185,027 \\).\n\nBut maybe easier: process digit by digit.\n\nStart with remainder \\( r = 0 \\).\n\nProcess digits of 4457185027:\n\n1. \\( r = 0 \\)  \nDigit 4: \\( r = (0 \\times 10 + 4) = 4 \\) \u2192 \\( 4 \\mod 257 = 4 \\).\n\n2. Digit 4: \\( r = (4 \\times 10 + 4) = 44 \\) \u2192 \\( 44 \\mod 257 = 44 \\).\n\n3. Digit 5: \\( r = (44 \\times 10 + 5) = 445 \\) \u2192 \\( 445 - 257 = 188 \\).\n\n4. Digit 7: \\( r = (188 \\times 10 + 7) = 1887 \\)  \n\\( 257 \\times 7 = 1799 \\), remainder \\( 1887 - 1799 = 88 \\).\n\n5. Digit 1: \\( r = (88 \\times 10 + 1) = 881 \\)  \n\\( 257 \\times 3 = 771 \\), remainder \\( 881 - 771 = 110 \\).\n\n6. Digit 8: \\( r = (110 \\times 10 + 8) = 1108 \\)  \n\\( 257 \\times 4 = 1028 \\), remainder \\( 1108 - 1028 = 80 \\).\n\n7. Digit 5: \\( r = (80 \\times 10 + 5) = 805 \\)  \n\\( 257 \\times 3 = 771 \\), remainder \\( 805 - 771 = 34 \\).\n\n8. Digit 0: \\( r = (34 \\times 10 + 0) = 340 \\)  \n\\( 340 - 257 = 83 \\).\n\n9. Digit 2: \\( r = (83 \\times 10 + 2) = 832 \\)  \n\\( 257 \\times 3 = 771 \\), remainder \\( 832 - 771 = 61 \\).\n\n10. Digit 7: \\( r = (61 \\times 10 + 7) = 617 \\)  \n\\( 257 \\times 2 = 514 \\), remainder \\( 617 - 514 = 103 \\).\n\n---\n\nSo the remainder is \\( 103 \\).\n\nLet\u2019s double-check quickly with another method:  \nWe can check \\( 4457185027 - 103 = 4457184924 \\). Divide by 257:  \n\\( 257 \\times 17343210 = 4457184970 \\) \u2014 wait, that\u2019s not matching. Let\u2019s check:\n\nActually, \\( 257 \\times 17343210 = 257 \\times (17,343,210) \\).  \n\\( 257 \\times 17,000,000 = 4,369,000,000 \\)  \n\\( 257 \\times 343,210 = 88,204,970 \\)  \nSum = \\( 4,457,204,970 \\), which is bigger than 4,457,184,924? Wait, that\u2019s wrong \u2014 I must check.\n\nBetter: \\( 4457185027 / 257 \\approx 17,343,132.4 \\). Multiply 257 \u00d7 17,343,132 = ?\n\n257 \u00d7 17,000,000 = 4,369,000,000  \n257 \u00d7 343,132 = 88,184,924  \nSum = 4,457,184,924. Yes, that matches 4457184924.  \nThen remainder = 4457185027 - 4457184924 = 103. Confirmed.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\nAnswer: 103\nConfidence: 100%"
