    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 9831076181 \\) is divided by \\( 215 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Break down the modulus**\n\n\\( 215 = 5 \\times 43 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder modulo 5 and modulo 43, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Modulo 5**\n\nA number mod 5 depends only on its last digit.  \nLast digit of \\( 9831076181 \\) is 1, so:\n\n\\[\n9831076181 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Modulo 43**\n\nWe need \\( 9831076181 \\bmod 43 \\).\n\nLet\u2019s do this step-by-step using modular reduction.\n\nFirst, note \\( 43 \\times 228000000 = 9804000000 \\).  \nDifference:  \n\\( 9831076181 - 9804000000 = 27076181 \\).\n\nNow reduce \\( 27076181 \\) mod 43.\n\n---\n\n43 \u00d7 600,000 = 25,800,000.  \nSubtract: \\( 27076181 - 25800000 = 1276181 \\).\n\n---\n\n43 \u00d7 29,000 = 1,247,000.  \nSubtract: \\( 1276181 - 1247000 = 29181 \\).\n\n---\n\n43 \u00d7 600 = 25,800.  \nSubtract: \\( 29181 - 25800 = 3381 \\).\n\n---\n\n43 \u00d7 78 = 3354.  \nSubtract: \\( 3381 - 3354 = 27 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 43 is 27.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Solve system**\n\nWe have:\n\\[\nx \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 27 \\pmod{43}\n\\]\n\nLet \\( x = 27 + 43k \\).  \nWe need \\( 27 + 43k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\n43 \u2261 3 mod 5, so:\n\n\\( 27 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\),  \n\\( 2 + 3k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\)  \n\\( 3k \\equiv -1 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\nMultiply both sides by inverse of 3 mod 5 (which is 2):  \n\\( k \\equiv 8 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\nSo \\( k = 3 + 5t \\).\n\nThen \\( x = 27 + 43(3 + 5t) = 27 + 129 + 215t = 156 + 215t \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Remainder between 0 and 214**\n\nThe smallest positive is \\( 156 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 6 \u2013 Check**\n\n156 mod 5 = 1 \u2705  \n156 mod 43: 43\u00d73=129, remainder 27 \u2705\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{156}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 156"
