    "raw": "Let\u2019s compute step-by-step.\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Modulo approach**  \nWe want \\( 9831076181 \\bmod 215 \\).\n\nFirst, note:  \n\\( 215 = 5 \\times 43 \\).\n\nWe can find remainder mod 5 and mod 43, then combine (Chinese Remainder Theorem).\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Mod 5:**  \nLast digit is 1, so remainder mod 5 is 1.\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Mod 43:**  \nWe find \\( 9831076181 \\bmod 43 \\).\n\nLet\u2019s do this stepwise:  \nFirst, 43 \u00d7 228,000,000 = 9,804,000,000.  \nDifference: 9,831,076,181 \u2212 9,804,000,000 = 27,076,181.\n\nNow reduce 27,076,181 mod 43:  \n43 \u00d7 629,000 = 27,047,000.  \nDifference: 27,076,181 \u2212 27,047,000 = 29,181.\n\n43 \u00d7 678 = 29,154.  \nDifference: 29,181 \u2212 29,154 = 27.  \n\nSo remainder mod 43 is 27.\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Solve system:**  \nWe have:  \n\\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 27 \\pmod{43} \\)\n\nLet \\( x = 27 + 43k \\).  \nMod 5: \\( 27 + 43k \\equiv 2 + 3k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\).  \nSo \\( 3k \\equiv -1 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\).  \nInverse of 3 mod 5 is 2 (since 3\u00d72=6\u22611).  \nMultiply: \\( k \\equiv 8 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\nSo k = 3 \u2192 x = 27 + 43\u00d73 = 27 + 129 = 156.  \nThis is less than 215, so remainder is 156.\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Check:**  \n156 mod 5 = 1 \u2705  \n156 mod 43 = 27 \u2705  \n\nSo remainder is 156.\n\nAnswer: 156  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nLet's compute step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\( 9831076181 \\mod 215 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\(215 = 5 \\times 43\\).\n\nWe can find the remainder mod 5 and mod 43, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Mod 5**\n\nThe last digit is 1, so:\n\n\\[\n9831076181 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 43**\n\nWe reduce 9831076181 mod 43.\n\nFirst, 43 \u00d7 228,000,000 = 9,804,000,000 \u2014 too big? Let's check:  \nActually, let's do stepwise division.\n\nCompute 43 \u00d7 228,629,678 = ?\n\nBetter: break the number.\n\nWe can use mod in parts:\n\nLet\u2019s take 9831076181 mod 43:\n\nFirst, 43 \u00d7 228,000,000 = 9,804,000,000.\n\nSubtract: 9,831,076,181 - 9,804,000,000 = 27,076,181.\n\nNow 27,076,181 mod 43:\n\n43 \u00d7 629,000 = 27,047,000.\n\nSubtract: 27,076,181 - 27,047,000 = 29,181.\n\nNow 29,181 mod 43:\n\n43 \u00d7 678 = 29,154.\n\n29,181 - 29,154 = 27.\n\nSo remainder mod 43 is 27.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Chinese Remainder Theorem**\n\nWe need \\(x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\\) and \\(x \\equiv 27 \\pmod{43}\\).\n\nFrom \\(x \\equiv 27 \\pmod{43}\\), possible x: 27, 70, 113, 156, 199, ... (adding 43 each time).\n\nWe need mod 5 = 1.\n\nCheck:\n\n- 27 mod 5 = 2 \u2192 no  \n- 70 mod 5 = 0 \u2192 no  \n- 113 mod 5 = 3 \u2192 no  \n- 156 mod 5 = 1 \u2192 yes.\n\nSo \\(x = 156\\) works.\n\nSince 156 < 215, this is the least positive remainder.\n\n---\n\nBut let's double-check: is 156 correct mod 215? Let's test directly:\n\n215 \u00d7 45,725,936 = ?\n\n215 \u00d7 45,000,000 = 9,675,000,000.  \nRemainder after that: 9,831,076,181 - 9,675,000,000 = 156,076,181.\n\nNow 215 \u00d7 726,000 = 156,090,000. That's slightly too big (156,090,000 > 156,076,181), so use 725,000:\n\n215 \u00d7 725,000 = 155,875,000.\n\nSubtract: 156,076,181 - 155,875,000 = 201,181.\n\nNow 215 \u00d7 935 = 201,025.\n\n201,181 - 201,025 = 156.\n\nYes, remainder 156.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\nAnswer: 156  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nFirst, note that \\( 215 = 5 \\times 43 \\).  \n\nWe can find the remainder modulo 5 and modulo 43, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Modulo 5:**  \nThe last digit is 1, so \\( 9831076181 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\n---\n\n**Modulo 43:**  \nWe need \\( 9831076181 \\bmod 43 \\).  \nBreak it into steps.\n\nFirst, note \\( 10^2 = 100 \\equiv 14 \\pmod{43} \\) (since \\( 100 - 86 = 14 \\)).  \nWe can reduce the number using modular powers.\n\nLet\u2019s compute step-by-step using the decimal digits.\n\nNumber: 9,831,076,181.\n\nWe can do it iteratively:\n\nStart with remainder \\( r = 0 \\).  \nProcess digits: 9, 8, 3, 1, 0, 7, 6, 1, 8, 1.\n\n1. r = (0\u00d710 + 9) mod 43 = 9  \n2. r = (9\u00d710 + 8) = 98 mod 43: 98 - 86 = 12  \n3. r = (12\u00d710 + 3) = 123 mod 43: 43\u00d72=86, 123-86=37  \n4. r = (37\u00d710 + 1) = 371 mod 43: 43\u00d78=344, remainder 27  \n5. r = (27\u00d710 + 0) = 270 mod 43: 43\u00d76=258, remainder 12  \n6. r = (12\u00d710 + 7) = 127 mod 43: 43\u00d72=86, remainder 41  \n7. r = (41\u00d710 + 6) = 416 mod 43: 43\u00d79=387, remainder 29  \n8. r = (29\u00d710 + 1) = 291 mod 43: 43\u00d76=258, remainder 33  \n9. r = (33\u00d710 + 8) = 338 mod 43: 43\u00d77=301, remainder 37  \n10. r = (37\u00d710 + 1) = 371 mod 43: as before remainder 27.\n\nSo \\( 9831076181 \\equiv 27 \\pmod{43} \\).\n\n---\n\n**Chinese Remainder Theorem:**  \nWe need \\( x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\) and \\( x \\equiv 27 \\pmod{43} \\).\n\nLet \\( x = 27 + 43k \\).  \nMod 5: \\( 27 \\equiv 2 \\), \\( 43 \\equiv 3 \\).  \nSo \\( 2 + 3k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\) \u2192 \\( 3k \\equiv -1 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\).  \nMultiply inverse of 3 mod 5: inverse is 2 (since 3\u00d72=6\u22611).  \nSo \\( k \\equiv 4\u00d72=8\u22613 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\nSmallest \\( k = 3 \\):  \n\\( x = 27 + 43\u00d73 = 27 + 129 = 156 \\).\n\nCheck: 156 mod 5 = 1, mod 43 = 27, correct.  \nSince 156 < 215, that's the remainder.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 156  \nConfidence: 95%\n---\nFirst, I'll compute \\( 9831076181 \\mod 215 \\).\n\nWe can use modular arithmetic step by step.  \n\nFirst, note \\( 215 = 5 \\times 43 \\).  \nWe can find the remainder modulo 5 and modulo 43, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Modulo 5:**  \nLast digit is 1, so remainder is \\( 1 \\mod 5 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Modulo 43:**  \nWe need \\( 9831076181 \\mod 43 \\).\n\nLet's do it stepwise:  \n\\( 43 \\times 228629678 = ? \\) That's too big to guess. Let's do it digit-by-digit or use modular reduction.\n\nInstead, break the number:  \nStart with remainder 0, process digits:\n\nNumber: 9 8 3 1 0 7 6 1 8 1\n\n- r = 0\n- digit 9: r = (0*10 + 9) = 9  \n- digit 8: r = (9*10 + 8) = 98 