\n- \\( 43 \\times 629,000 = 27,047,000 \\)  \nDifference: \\( 27,076,181 - 27,047,000 = 29,181 \\).\n\n- \\( 43 \\times 678 = 29,154 \\)  \nDifference: \\( 29,181 - 29,154 = 27 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 43 is 27.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Solve system**\n\nWe have:\n\\[\nx \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 27 \\pmod{43}\n\\]\n\nLet \\( x = 27 + 43k \\).  \nMod 5: \\( 27 + 43k \\equiv 2 + 3k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\).  \nSo \\( 3k \\equiv -1 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\nInverse of 3 mod 5 is 2 (since \\(3\\times2=6\\equiv1\\)).  \nMultiply: \\( k \\equiv 4\\times 2 = 8 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\nSo \\( k = 3 + 5t \\).  \nThen \\( x = 27 + 43(3+5t) = 27 + 129 + 215t = 156 + 215t \\).\n\nThus remainder is \\( 156 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Check:**  \n156 mod 5 = 1 \u2705  \n156 mod 43: \\( 43\\times3=129\\), remainder \\(27\\) \u2705  \n\nAlso 156 < 215, so it's the remainder.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 156  \nConfidence: 95%"
