    "raw": "Let\u2019s go step-by-step.\n\nWe need the remainder of \\( 63438575 \\div 637 \\).\n\nFirst, approximate:\n\n\\( 637 \\times 100000 = 63,700,000 \\) which is slightly more than 63,438,575.\n\nLet\u2019s try \\( 637 \\times 99500 \\):\n\n- \\( 637 \\times 100000 = 63,700,000 \\)\n- Subtract \\( 637 \\times 500 = 318,500 \\)\n- So \\( 63,700,000 - 318,500 = 63,381,500 \\)\n\nDifference from 63,438,575:  \n\\( 63,438,575 - 63,381,500 = 57,075 \\)\n\nNow see how many more times 637 fits into 57,075:\n\n- \\( 637 \\times 89 = 637 \\times 90 - 637 = 57,330 - 637 = 56,693 \\)\n- Remainder after that: \\( 57,075 - 56,693 = 382 \\)\n\n382 is less than 637, so that\u2019s the remainder.\n\nLet\u2019s verify:  \nTotal quotient = \\( 99,500 + 89 = 99,589 \\)  \n\\( 637 \\times 99,589 = 63,438,193 \\)  \nDifference from 63,438,575 = \\( 382 \\). \u2705\n\n**Answer:** 382  \n**Confidence:** 100%  \n\nAnswer: 382  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet\u2019s go step-by-step.\n\nWe need to find \\( 63438575 \\mod 637 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 637 = 7^2 \\times 13 \\)? Let's check:  \n\\( 7^2 = 49\\), \\(49 \\times 13 = 637\\). Yes.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Divide 63438575 by 637.**\n\nWe can do this by long division or modular reduction.\n\nFirst, let's see roughly how many times 637 goes into 63438575.\n\n- \\(637 \\times 100,000 = 63,700,000\\)  \nDifference: \\(63,438,575 - 63,700,000\\) \u2014 wait, that\u2019s negative. So 100,000 times is too big. Let's try smaller.\n\nActually \\(63438575 \\approx 63.4\\) million, \\(637 \\times 100,000 = 63,700,000\\) is bigger. So try \\(99,000\\):\n\n\\(637 \\times 99,000 = 637 \\times (100,000 - 1,000) = 63,700,000 - 637,000 = 63,063,000\\).\n\nDifference: \\(63,438,575 - 63,063,000 = 375,575\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Divide 375,575 by 637.**\n\n\\(637 \\times 500 = 318,500\\)  \nDifference: \\(375,575 - 318,500 = 57,075\\).\n\n\\(637 \\times 80 = 50,960\\)  \nDifference: \\(57,075 - 50,960 = 6,115\\).\n\n\\(637 \\times 9 = 5,733\\)  \nDifference: \\(6,115 - 5,733 = 382\\).\n\n382 is less than 637. So remainder is 382.\n\n---\n\nLet's quickly check:  \nWe had \\(99,000 + 500 + 80 + 9 = 99,589\\) as quotient.  \n\\(637 \\times 99,589 = ?\\)\n\n\\(637 \\times 99,589 = 637 \\times (100,000 - 411) = 63,700,000 - (637 \\times 411)\\)  \n\\(637 \\times 411 = 637 \\times 400 + 637 \\times 11 = 254,800 + 7,007 = 261,807\\).  \nSubtract: \\(63,700,000 - 261,807 = 63,438,193\\).  \nAdd remainder 382 \u2192 \\(63,438,193 + 382 = 63,438,575\\). Matches.\n\nSo remainder = 382.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 382  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 63438575 \\mod 637 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 637 = 7^2 \\times 13 \\).  \nBut instead of factoring, let's just do the modular division.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Estimate quotient**  \n637 \u00d7 100,000 = 63,700,000, which is slightly less than 63,438,575.\n\nDifference:  \n63,438,575 \u2212 63,700,000 = \u2212261,425. This means 100,000 is too big, so start with 99,000.\n\n637 \u00d7 99,000 = 637 \u00d7 (100,000 \u2212 1,000) = 63,700,000 \u2212 637,000 = 63,063,000.\n\nDifference: 63,438,575 \u2212 63,063,000 = 375,575.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Divide remainder 375,575 by 637.**\n\n637 \u00d7 500 = 318,500. Subtract: 375,575 \u2212 318,500 = 57,075.\n\n637 \u00d7 80 = 50,960. Subtract: 57,075 \u2212 50,960 = 6,115.\n\n637 \u00d7 9 = 5,733. Subtract: 6,115 \u2212 5,733 = 382.\n\n382 < 637, so remainder is 382.\n\n---\n\nCheck: 637 \u00d7 99,589 = 637 \u00d7 (99,000 + 589) = 63,063,000 + (637 \u00d7 589).  \n637 \u00d7 589 = 637 \u00d7 (600 \u2212 11) = 382,200 \u2212 7,007 = 375,193.  \n\nAdd: 63,063,000 + 375,193 = 63,438,193.  \n63,438,575 \u2212 63,438,193 = 382. Correct.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nAnswer: 382  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 63438575 \\mod 637 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 637 = 7 \\times 91 = 7 \\times 7 \\times 13 = 49 \\times 13 \\).\n\nWe can do the division step-by-step.\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Estimate the quotient:**\n\\( 637 \\times 100000 = 