    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 99721481 \\) is divided by \\( 875 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Note the modulus factorization**\n\n\\( 875 = 7 \\times 125 = 7 \\times 5^3 \\).\n\nWe could use the Chinese Remainder Theorem, but direct division might be simpler here.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Try direct division approach**\n\nWe can find \\( 99721481 \\mod 875 \\) by breaking it into parts.\n\nFirst, note \\( 1000 \\equiv 125 \\pmod{875} \\) because \\(1000 - 875 = 125\\).\n\nBut maybe easier: Let's find \\( 99721481 \\mod 875 \\) by using that \\( 875 \\times 100000 = 87500000 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Subtract the big multiple**\n\n\\( 99721481 - 87500000 = 12221481 \\).\n\nNow we need \\( 12221481 \\mod 875 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Another big multiple**\n\n\\( 875 \\times 10000 = 8750000 \\).\n\n\\( 12221481 - 8750000 = 3471481 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Another multiple**\n\n\\( 875 \\times 3000 = 2625000 \\).\n\n\\( 3471481 - 2625000 = 846481 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 6 \u2013 Another multiple**\n\n\\( 875 \\times 900 = 787500 \\).\n\n\\( 846481 - 787500 = 58981 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 7 \u2013 Another multiple**\n\n\\( 875 \\times 60 = 52500 \\).\n\n\\( 58981 - 52500 = 6481 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 8 \u2013 Another multiple**\n\n\\( 875 \\times 7 = 6125 \\).\n\n\\( 6481 - 6125 = 356 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 9 \u2013 Check if 356 < 875**\n\nYes, 356 is less than 875, so this is the remainder.\n\n---\n\n**Step 10 \u2013 Final check**\n\nWe can verify: \\( 875 \\times 113967 = ? \\)  \nActually, let's check mod quickly:  \n\\( 99721481 - 356 = 99721125 \\).  \nDivide by 875: \\( 99721125 / 875 = 113967 \\) exactly?  \n875 \u00d7 113967 = 875 \u00d7 (114000 - 33) = 99750000 - 28875 = 99721125. Yes.\n\nSo remainder is indeed 356.\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 356"
