    "raw": "Let's compute step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 74940010 \\) is divided by \\( 828 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Check divisibility by 4**  \n828 = 4 \u00d7 207.  \nLast two digits of 74940010 are 10, which is not divisible by 4, so the number is not divisible by 4. But we don't need divisibility, just remainder.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Use modular arithmetic**  \nWe can break 828 into factors: \\( 828 = 4 \\times 207 = 4 \\times 9 \\times 23 \\).  \nBut direct division might be simpler.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Direct division approach**  \nFirst, approximate:  \n828 \u00d7 90,000 = 74,520,000.  \nDifference: 74,940,010 \u2212 74,520,000 = 420,010.\n\nNow divide 420,010 by 828:  \n828 \u00d7 500 = 414,000.  \nRemainder: 420,010 \u2212 414,000 = 6,010.\n\nNow divide 6,010 by 828:  \n828 \u00d7 7 = 5,796.  \nRemainder: 6,010 \u2212 5,796 = 214.\n\nSo total quotient = 90,000 + 500 + 7 = 90,507, remainder 214.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Check**  \n828 \u00d7 90,507 = 828 \u00d7 90,000 + 828 \u00d7 507.  \n828 \u00d7 90,000 = 74,520,000.  \n828 \u00d7 507 = 828 \u00d7 500 + 828 \u00d7 7 = 414,000 + 5,796 = 419,796.  \nSum = 74,520,000 + 419,796 = 74,939,796.  \nAdd remainder 214 \u2192 74,940,010. \u2705\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:** 214.\n\nAnswer: 214  \nConfidence: 100%"
