    "raw": "Probability: 85%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 74940010 \\) is divided by \\( 828 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Check divisibility rules and simplify if possible.**\n\nFirst, note \\( 828 = 4 \\times 207 = 4 \\times 9 \\times 23 \\).  \nSo \\( 828 = 2^2 \\times 3^2 \\times 23 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder modulo \\( 828 \\) by using the Chinese Remainder Theorem with moduli \\( 4 \\), \\( 9 \\), and \\( 23 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Modulo 4.**\n\nThe last two digits of \\( 74940010 \\) are \\( 10 \\), and \\( 10 \\mod 4 = 2 \\).  \nSo remainder mod 4 is \\( 2 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Modulo 9.**\n\nSum of digits of \\( 74940010 \\):\n\n\\( 7+4+9+4+0+0+1+0 = 25 \\).  \n\\( 25 \\mod 9 = 7 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 9 is \\( 7 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Modulo 23.**\n\nWe need \\( 74940010 \\mod 23 \\).\n\nFirst reduce 74940010 stepwise.\n\nLet\u2019s compute \\( 10^6 \\mod 23 \\) maybe? But easier: break the number.\n\n74940010 = \\( 7494 \\times 10000 + 10 \\) maybe? Let's check:  \n\\( 7494 \\times 10000 = 74940000 \\), plus 10 gives 74940010. Yes.\n\nSo compute mod 23:\n\nFirst, \\( 10000 \\mod 23 \\):  \n23 \u00d7 434 = 9982, remainder 18. So \\( 10000 \\equiv 18 \\mod 23 \\).\n\nNow \\( 7494 \\mod 23 \\):\n\n23 \u00d7 325 = 7475, remainder 19. So \\( 7494 \\equiv 19 \\mod 23 \\).\n\nThus \\( 7494 \\times 10000 \\equiv 19 \\times 18 = 342 \\).  \n342 mod 23: 23 \u00d7 14 = 322, remainder 20.\n\nThen add 10: \\( 20 + 10 = 30 \\), and \\( 30 \\mod 23 = 7 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 23 is \\( 7 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Solve CRT.**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\( x \\equiv 2 \\pmod{4} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{9} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{23} \\)\n\nFrom the last two: \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{9} \\) and \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{23} \\) means \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{\\mathrm{lcm}(9,23)} \\).  \nSince 9 and 23 are coprime, lcm = 207. So \\( x \\equiv 7 \\pmod{207} \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 6: Combine with mod 4 condition.**\n\nLet \\( x = 7 + 207k \\).  \nMod 4: \\( 7 \\equiv 3 \\), \\( 207 \\equiv 3 \\) mod 4 (since 204 divisible by 4, remainder 3).  \nSo \\( x \\equiv 3 + 3k \\pmod{4} \\). We want this \u2261 2 mod 4.\n\nSo \\( 3 + 3k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{4} \\)  \n\\( 3k \\equiv -1 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4} \\).\n\nMultiply both sides by inverse of 3 mod 4 (which is 3):  \n\\( k \\equiv 9 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4} \\).\n\nSo \\( k = 1 + 4t \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 7: Find x.**\n\n\\( x = 7 + 207(1 + 4t) = 7 + 207 + 828t = 214 + 828t \\).\n\nThus remainder is \\( 214 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 8: Check if less than 828** \u2014 yes, 214 < 828.\n\n---\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{214}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 214"
