es (100 + 28) = 923,800,000 + 258,664,000 \\).\n- \\( 9,238,000 \\times 28 = 9,238,000 \\times (30 - 2) = 277,140,000 - 18,476,000 = 258,664,000 \\). Correct.\n- Sum: \\( 923,800,000 + 258,664,000 = 1,182,464,000 \\).\n- Double it: \\( 2,364,928,000 \\).\n\nFinally \\( 128^2 = 16,384 \\).\n\nNow sum:\n\n\\( 85,340,644,000,000 + 2,364,928,000 = 85,343,008,928,000 \\).\n\nAdd \\( 16,384 \\):\n\n\\( 85,343,008,944,384 \\).\n\nSo the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{85343008944384}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 85343008944384\nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 9238128^2 \\).\n\nWe can use the identity \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\).  \nLet \\( a = 9,238,000 \\) and \\( b = 128 \\).\n\n- \\( a^2 = (9,238,000)^2 \\)  \nFirst, \\( 9,238^2 \\):\n  - \\( 9,238^2 = (9,200 + 38)^2 = 9,200^2 + 2 \\cdot 9,200 \\cdot 38 + 38^2 \\)\n  - \\( 9,200^2 = 84,640,000 \\)\n  - \\( 2 \\cdot 9,200 \\cdot 38 = 18,400 \\cdot 38 = 699,200 \\)\n  - \\( 38^2 = 1,444 \\)\n  - Sum: \\( 84,640,000 + 699,200 + 1,444 = 85,340,644 \\)\n- Multiply by \\( 1,000,000 \\) (since \\( 9,238,000 = 9,238 \\times 1000 \\), square gives \\( \\times 1,000,000 \\)):  \n\\( a^2 = 85,340,644,000,000 \\).\n\n- \\( 2ab = 2 \\cdot 9,238,000 \\cdot 128 \\)  \nFirst \\( 9,238,000 \\cdot 128 = 9,238,000 \\cdot (100 + 28) \\)  \n\\( = 923,800,000 + 9,238,000 \\cdot 28 \\)  \n\\( 9,238,000 \\cdot 28 = 9,238,000 \\cdot (30 - 2) = 277,140,000 - 18,476,000 = 258,664,000 \\)  \nSum: \\( 923,800,000 + 258,664,000 = 1,182,464,000 \\)  \nMultiply by 2: \\( 2ab = 2,364,928,000 \\).\n\n- \\( b^2 = 128^2 = 16,384 \\).\n\nNow sum:  \n\\( a^2 + 2ab + b^2 = 85,340,644,000,000 + 2,364,928,000 + 16,384 \\)  \nFirst add \\( a^2 + 2ab \\): \\( 85,340,644,000,000 + 2,364,928,000 = 85,343,008,928,000 \\)  \nThen add \\( 16,384 \\): \\( 85,343,008,944,384 \\).\n\nSo \\( 9238128^2 = 85,343,008,944,384 \\).\n\nAnswer: 85343008944384  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute \\( 9238128^2 \\).\n\nWe can do this step-by-step:\n\n- Let \\( a = 9,238,128 \\).\