 = \\( 85,343,008,944,384 \\). Same result.\n\nAnswer: 85343008944384\nConfidence: 100%\n---\nAlright, let's compute \\( 9,238,128^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\nWe can use the identity:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nLet\u2019s take:\n\n- \\( a = 9,200,000 \\)\n- \\( b = 38,128 \\)\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Compute \\( a^2 \\)**\n\n\\[\n9,200,000^2 = (92 \\times 10^5)^2 = 92^2 \\times 10^{10}\n\\]\n\\[\n92^2 = 8464\n\\]\nSo:\n\\[\na^2 = 8464 \\times 10^{10} = 84,640,000,000,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Compute \\( 2ab \\)**\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 9,200,000 \\times 38,128\n\\]\nFirst \\( 9,200,000 \\times 38,128 \\):\n\n\\( 9,200,000 \\times 38,000 = 349,600,000,000 \\)  \n\\( 9,200,000 \\times 128 = 1,177,600,000 \\)  \nSum: \\( 349,600,000,000 + 1,177,600,000 = 350,777,600,000 \\)\n\nMultiply by 2:\n\\[\n2ab = 701,555,200,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Compute \\( b^2 \\)**\n\n\\[\n38,128^2\n\\]\nLet\u2019s do \\( (38,000 + 128)^2 \\):\n\n\\( 38,000^2 = 1,444,000,000 \\)  \n\\( 2 \\times 38,000 \\times 128 = 76,000 \\times 128 = 9,728,000 \\)  \n\\( 128^2 = 16,384 \\)\n\nSum:\n\\[\n1,444,000,000 + 9,728,000 + 16,384 = 1,453,744,384\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Add them together**\n\n\\[\na^2 = 84,640,000,000,000\n\\]\n\\[\n2ab = 701,555,200,000\n\\]\n\\[\nb^2 = 1,453,744,384\n\\]\n\nFirst \\( a^2 + 2ab \\):\n\\[\n84,640,000,000,000 + 701,555,200,000 = 85,341,555,200,000\n\\]\n\nNow add \\( b^2 \\):\n\\[\n85,341,555,200,000 + 1,453,744,384 = 85,343,008,944,384\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{85343008944384}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 85343008944384\nConfidence: 98%"
