ainder 16  \n163 \u2192 163 mod 47: 47\u00d73=141, remainder 22.\n\nSo remainder mod 47 is 22.  \nCheck 521 mod 47: 47\u00d711=517, remainder 4. Uh-oh, mismatch! So maybe I made an error in mod 47 calculation.\n\nLet's recompute mod 47 carefully:\n\nNumber: 6714205543.\n\nProcess digits:\n\nStart r=0.  \nDigit 6: r = (0\u00d710+6) = 6.  \nDigit 7: r = (6\u00d710+7)=67 \u2192 67\u221247=20.  \nDigit 1: r = (20\u00d710+1)=201 \u2192 201\u2212188=13.  \nDigit 4: r = (13\u00d710+4)=134 \u2192 134\u221294=40.  \nDigit 2: r = (40\u00d710+2)=402 \u2192 402\u2212376=26.  \nDigit 0: r = (26\u00d710+0)=260 \u2192 260\u2212235=25.  \nDigit 5: r = (25\u00d710+5)=255 \u2192 255\u2212235=20.  \nDigit 5: r = (20\u00d710+5)=205 \u2192 205\u2212188=17 (I earlier wrote 204, mistake!).  \nDigit 4: r = (17\u00d710+4)=174 \u2192 174\u2212141=33.  \nDigit 3: r = (33\u00d710+3)=333 \u2192 333\u2212329=4.\n\nSo remainder mod 47 is 4. That matches 521 mod 47 = 4. Good.\n\nCheck mod 2: 521 is odd, matches.\n\nSo remainder is 521.\n\nAnswer: 521  \nConfidence: 100%"
