    "raw": "Alright, let's compute \\( 2562287^2 \\) step-by-step.\n\nWe can use the identity:  \n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\nLet\u2019s take \\( a = 2560000 \\) and \\( b = 2287 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Compute \\( a^2 \\)**\n\\[\n2560000^2 = (256^2) \\times 10^8\n\\]\n\\( 256^2 = 65536 \\), so:\n\\[\n65536 \\times 10^8 = 6,553,600,000,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Compute \\( 2ab \\)**\n\\[\n2 \\times 2560000 \\times 2287\n\\]\nFirst, \\( 2560000 \\times 2287 = 256 \\times 2287 \\times 10^4 \\).\n\n\\( 256 \\times 2287 \\):\n- \\( 2287 \\times 200 = 457,400 \\)\n- \\( 2287 \\times 50 = 114,350 \\)\n- \\( 2287 \\times 6 = 13,722 \\)\n\nSum: \\( 457,400 + 114,350 = 571,750 \\), plus \\( 13,722 \\) gives \\( 585,472 \\).\n\nSo \\( 2560000 \\times 2287 = 585,472 \\times 10^4 = 5,854,720,000 \\).\n\nMultiply by 2:\n\\[\n2ab = 11,709,440,000\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Compute \\( b^2 \\)**\n\\[\n2287^2\n\\]\nUse \\( (2300 - 13)^2 = 2300^2 - 2 \\times 2300 \\times 13 + 13^2 \\).\n\n\\( 2300^2 = 5,290,000 \\)  \n\\( 2 \\times 2300 \\times 13 = 59,800 \\)  \n\\( 13^2 = 169 \\)\n\nSo:\n\\[\n5,290,000 - 59,800 + 169 = 5,230,369\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Add them up**\n\\[\na^2 = 6,553,600,000,000\n\\]\n\\[\n2ab = 11,709,440,000\n\\]\n\\[\nb^2 = 5,230,369\n\\]\n\nFirst sum \\( a^2 + 2ab \\):\n\\[\n6,553,600,000,000 + 11,709,440,000 = 6,565,309,440,000\n\\]\n\nNow add \\( b^2 \\):\n\\[\n6,565,309,440,000 + 5,230,369 = 6,565,314,670,369\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{6565314670369}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 6565314670369  \nConfidence: 95%"
