    "raw": "Let's compute step-by-step.\n\nWe want \\( 99892850 \\mod 415 \\).\n\nFirst, note \\( 415 = 5 \\times 83 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Mod 5**\n\n99892850 ends with 0, so it's divisible by 5.  \nRemainder mod 5 = 0.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 83**\n\nWe can reduce 99892850 mod 83.\n\nFirst, 83 \u00d7 1,000,000 = 83,000,000.  \n99892850 \u2212 83,000,000 = 16,892,850.\n\n83 \u00d7 200,000 = 16,600,000.  \n16,892,850 \u2212 16,600,000 = 292,850.\n\n83 \u00d7 3,000 = 249,000.  \n292,850 \u2212 249,000 = 43,850.\n\n83 \u00d7 500 = 41,500.  \n43,850 \u2212 41,500 = 2,350.\n\n83 \u00d7 28 = 2,324.  \n2,350 \u2212 2,324 = 26.\n\nSo remainder mod 83 = 26.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Solve system**\n\nWe need \\( x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5} \\) and \\( x \\equiv 26 \\pmod{83} \\).\n\nLet \\( x = 5k \\). Then \\( 5k \\equiv 26 \\pmod{83} \\).\n\nFind inverse of 5 mod 83:  \n5 \u00d7 17 = 85 \u2261 2 mod 83, not 1.  \n5 \u00d7 50 = 250 \u2261 250 \u2212 249 = 1 mod 83. So inverse is 50.\n\nThus \\( k \\equiv 26 \\times 50 = 1300 \\pmod{83} \\).\n\n1300 \u00f7 83: 83 \u00d7 15 = 1245, remainder 55. So \\( k \\equiv 55 \\pmod{83} \\).\n\nThus \\( x = 5k = 5(55 + 83t) = 275 + 415t \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 415 is 275.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Check**\n\n275 mod 5 = 0 \u2705  \n275 mod 83: 83 \u00d7 3 = 249, remainder 26 \u2705\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\n\nAnswer: 275  \nConfidence: 100%"
