    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 99892850 \\) is divided by \\( 415 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Check divisibility or simplify the problem**\n\nFirst, note that \\( 415 = 5 \\times 83 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder mod 5 and mod 83, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Mod 5**\n\nThe last digit of \\( 99892850 \\) is 0, so it's divisible by 5.\n\nRemainder mod 5 = 0.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Mod 83**\n\nWe need \\( 99892850 \\bmod 83 \\).\n\nLet's do this step-by-step.\n\nFirst, break the number: \\( 99892850 \\).\n\nWe can reduce using mod 83.\n\n---\n\n**Method: Use modular reduction directly.**\n\n83 \u00d7 1,000,000 = 83,000,000.  \nSubtract: \\( 99,892,850 - 83,000,000 = 16,892,850 \\).\n\nNow reduce 16,892,850 mod 83.\n\n83 \u00d7 200,000 = 16,600,000.  \nSubtract: \\( 16,892,850 - 16,600,000 = 292,850 \\).\n\n83 \u00d7 3,000 = 249,000.  \nSubtract: \\( 292,850 - 249,000 = 43,850 \\).\n\n83 \u00d7 500 = 41,500.  \nSubtract: \\( 43,850 - 41,500 = 2,350 \\).\n\n83 \u00d7 28 = 2,324.  \nSubtract: \\( 2,350 - 2,324 = 26 \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 83 is 26.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Solve system**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\( x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 26 \\pmod{83} \\)\n\nLet \\( x = 5k \\). Then \\( 5k \\equiv 26 \\pmod{83} \\).\n\nFind inverse of 5 mod 83:  \n83 = 16\u00d75 + 3  \n5 = 1\u00d73 + 2  \n3 = 1\u00d72 + 1  \nBack substitute:  \n1 = 3 - 1\u00d72  \n2 = 5 - 1\u00d73  \nSo 1 = 3 - (5 - 3) = 2\u00d73 - 5  \n3 = 83 - 16\u00d75  \nSo 1 = 2\u00d7(83 - 16\u00d75) - 5 = 2\u00d783 - 32\u00d75 - 5 = 2\u00d783 - 33\u00d75.\n\nThus -33\u00d75 \u2261 1 mod 83, so inverse of 5 is -33 \u2261 50 mod 83.\n\nMultiply: \\( k \\equiv 26 \\times 50 \\pmod{83} \\).  \n26\u00d750 = 1300.  \n83\u00d715 = 1245, remainder 55.\n\nSo \\( k \\equiv 55 \\pmod{83} \\).\n\nThus \\( x = 5k = 5(55 + 83t) = 275 + 415t \\).\n\nSo remainder mod 415 is 275.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5: Check**\n\n275 mod 5 = 0 \u2705  \n275 mod 83: 83\u00d73=249, remainder 26 \u2705\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\n\nAnswer: 275"
