 2 \u2013 Further divide the difference:**\n\n\\( 922 \\times 200,000 = 184,400,000 \\)  \nRemainder after that: \\( 201,018,738 - 184,400,000 = 16,618,738 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Continue:**\n\n\\( 922 \\times 18,000 = 16,596,000 \\)  \nRemainder: \\( 16,618,738 - 16,596,000 = 22,738 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Continue:**\n\n\\( 922 \\times 24 = 22,128 \\)  \nRemainder: \\( 22,738 - 22,128 = 610 \\).\n\nSince \\( 610 < 922 \\), we stop.\n\n---\n\nSo the remainder is \\( 610 \\).\n\n**Final check:**  \nQuotient total = \\( 10,000,000 + 200,000 + 18,000 + 24 = 10,218,024 \\).  \nMultiply: \\( 10,218,024 \\times 922 = 9,421,018,128 \\).  \nAdd remainder: \\( 9,421,018,128 + 610 = 9,421,018,738 \\). \u2705\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 610  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's compute the remainder when \\( 9421018738 \\) is divided by \\( 922 \\).\n\nWe can perform modular division step-by-step.\n\nFirst, note \\( 922 \\times 10,000,000 = 9,220,000,000 \\), which is less than \\( 9,421,018,738 \\).\n\nDifference:  \n\\( 9,421,018,738 - 9,220,000,000 = 201,018,738 \\).\n\nSo \\( 9,421,018,738 \\mod 922 = 201,018,738 \\mod 922 \\).\n\nNow, \\( 922 \\times 200,000 = 184,400,000 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 201,018,738 - 184,400,000 = 16,618,738 \\).\n\nNext, \\( 922 \\times 18,000 = 16,596,000 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 16,618,738 - 16,596,000 = 22,738 \\).\n\nNext, \\( 922 \\times 20 = 18,440 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 22,738 - 18,440 = 4,298 \\).\n\nNext, \\( 922 \\times 4 = 3,688 \\).  \nSubtract: \\( 4,298 - 3,688 = 610 \\).\n\nSince \\( 610 < 922 \\), the remainder is \\( 610 \\).\n\nAnswer: 610  \nConfidence: 100%\n---\nLet's go through the problem step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder of \\( 9421018738 \\div 922 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 First, check divisibility rules or reduce the problem.**\n\nNote that:\n\n\\[\n922 = 2 \\times 461\n\\]\nSince 461 is prime (check: not divisible by 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19; \\(\\sqrt{461} \\approx 21.47\\), so check primes up to 19 \u2014 461/13 \u2248 35.46 not integer, 461/17 \u2248 27.117, 461/19 \u2248 24.26 \u2014 so yes, prime).\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Use modular arithmetic.**\n\nWe can find \\(9421018738 \\bmod 922\\).\n\nFirst, break 922 = 2 \u00d7 461, and note the number is even (ends with 8), so mod 2 = 0. We'll use this in the end.\n\nLet\u2019s find the remainder mod 461, then combine.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Compute \\(9421018738 \\bmod 461\\).**\n\nFirst, reduce 9421018738 modulo 461.\n\nLet\u2019s see 461 \u00d7 20,000,000 = 9,220,000,000.  \nDifference: 9,421,018,738 \u2212 9,220,000,000 = 201,018,738.\n\nNow reduce 201,018,738 mod 461.\n\n461 \u00d7 436,000 = 461 \u00d7 436 \u00d7 1000.  \n461 \u00d7 436 = 461 \u00d7 400 + 461 \u00d7 36 = 184,400 + 16,596 = 200,996.  \nTimes 1000 \u2192 200,996,000.\n\nDifference: 201,018,738 \u2212 200,996,000 = 22,738.\n\nNow reduce 22,738 mod 461.\n\n461 \u00d7 49 = 461 \u00d7 50 \u2212 461 = 23,050 \u2212 461 = 22,589.\n\n22,738 \u2212 22,589 = 149.\n\nSo remainder mod 461 is 149.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Combine with mod 2 condition.**\n\nWe have:\n\n\\( x \\equiv 149 \\pmod{461} \\)  \n\\( x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2} \\).\n\nWe need x mod 922.\n\nCheck 149 mod 2 = 1 (odd), so not matching. Add 461 to 149 \u2192 610 (even). So 610 mod 2 = 0.\n\nThus remainder mod 922 is 610.\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Double-check with direct calculation (mental estimate).**\n\n922 \u00d7 10,000,000 = 9,220,000,000, difference = 201,018,738 (same as before).\n\n922 \u00d7 218,000 = 922 \u00d7 218 \u00d7 1000.  \n922 \u00d7 218 = 922 \u00d7 200 + 922 \u00d7 18 = 184,400 + 16,596 = 200,996. Times 1000 \u2192 200,996,000.\n\nDifference = 22,738.\n\n922 \u00d7 24 = 22,128.  \n22,738 \u2212 22,128 = 610.\n\nYes, remainder is 610.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:**\n\nAnswer: 610  \nConfidence: 100%"
