    "raw": "Let's compute \\( 11245123 \\mod 133 \\).\n\nFirst, note that \\( 133 = 7 \\times 19 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder modulo 7 and modulo 19, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Modulo 7**\n\nFirst, \\( 11245123 \\mod 7 \\).\n\nWe can do this step-by-step:\n\n- \\( 11 \\mod 7 = 4 \\)\n- Bring down 2 \u2192 42, \\( 42 \\mod 7 = 0 \\)\n- Bring down 4 \u2192 4, \\( 4 \\mod 7 = 4 \\)\n- Bring down 5 \u2192 45, \\( 45 \\mod 7 = 3 \\)\n- Bring down 1 \u2192 31, \\( 31 \\mod 7 = 3 \\)\n- Bring down 2 \u2192 32, \\( 32 \\mod 7 = 4 \\)\n- Bring down 3 \u2192 43, \\( 43 \\mod 7 = 1 \\)\n\nSo remainder mod 7 is 1.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Modulo 19**\n\nCompute \\( 11245123 \\mod 19 \\).\n\nLet's do it stepwise:\n\n- 11 mod 19 = 11\n- Bring down 2 \u2192 112, \\( 112 \\mod 19 \\): \\( 19\\times5=95\\), remainder 17\n- Bring down 4 \u2192 174, \\( 19\\times9=171\\), remainder 3\n- Bring down 5 \u2192 35, remainder 16\n- Bring down 1 \u2192 161, \\( 19\\times8=152\\), remainder 9\n- Bring down 2 \u2192 92, \\( 19\\times4=76\\), remainder 16\n- Bring down 3 \u2192 163, \\( 19\\times8=152\\), remainder 11\n\nSo remainder mod 19 is 11.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Solve system**\n\nWe have:\n\\[\nx \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\equiv 11 \\pmod{19}\n\\]\n\nFrom the first, \\( x = 1 + 7k \\).\n\nSub into second: \\( 1 + 7k \\equiv 11 \\pmod{19} \\)  \n\\( 7k \\equiv 10 \\pmod{19} \\).\n\nFind inverse of 7 mod 19: \\( 7\\times 11 = 77 \\equiv 1 \\mod 19 \\) (since 76 is multiple of 19). So inverse is 11.\n\nMultiply both sides by 11: \\( k \\equiv 110 \\mod 19 \\).  \n\\( 110 - 19\\times5 = 110 - 95 = 15 \\).\n\nSo \\( k \\equiv 15 \\pmod{19} \\).\n\nThus \\( x = 1 + 7\\times 15 = 1 + 105 = 106 \\).\n\nCheck: 106 mod 7 = 1, 106 mod 19 = 106 - 95 = 11. Good.\n\nSince 106 < 133, that's the remainder.\n\n---\n\n**Final answer:** 106\n\nAnswer: 106  \nConfidence: 95%"
