    "raw": "Probability: 85%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 11245123 \\) is divided by \\( 133 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Check divisibility or break down the modulus**\n\nFirst, note that \\( 133 = 7 \\times 19 \\).  \nWe could find the remainder mod 7 and mod 19, then use the Chinese Remainder Theorem. But maybe direct division is simpler here.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Try direct long division**\n\nWe can do it directly:\n\n- \\( 133 \\times 80000 = 10,640,000 \\)  \n  Subtract from 11,245,123:  \n  \\( 11,245,123 - 10,640,000 = 605,123 \\).\n\n- \\( 133 \\times 4000 = 532,000 \\)  \n  Subtract: \\( 605,123 - 532,000 = 73,123 \\).\n\n- \\( 133 \\times 500 = 66,500 \\)  \n  Subtract: \\( 73,123 - 66,500 = 6,623 \\).\n\n- \\( 133 \\times 49 = 6517 \\) (since \\( 133 \\times 50 = 6650\\), minus 133 = 6517)  \n  Subtract: \\( 6,623 - 6,517 = 106 \\).\n\n106 is less than 133, so remainder is 106.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Verify with modular arithmetic**\n\nLet\u2019s check mod 7 and mod 19:\n\n- Mod 7:  \n  \\( 11245123 \\mod 7 \\):  \n  7 \u00d7 1,606,446 = 11,245,122, remainder 1. So \u2261 1 mod 7.\n\n- Mod 19:  \n  19 \u00d7 591,848 = 11,245,112, remainder 11. So \u2261 11 mod 19.\n\nNow check 106:  \n106 mod 7 = 1 (since 105 is divisible by 7). \u2705  \n106 mod 19: 19 \u00d7 5 = 95, remainder 11. \u2705\n\nSo 106 matches both.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Conclusion**\n\nThe remainder is \\( 106 \\).\n\n---\n\nAnswer: 106"
