    "raw": "Probability: 95%\n---\nAlright, let's go step-by-step.\n\nWe want the remainder when \\( 74309920 \\) is divided by \\( 165 \\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Factor the divisor**  \n\\( 165 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 11 \\).\n\nWe can find the remainder modulo \\(165\\) by finding remainders modulo \\(3\\), \\(5\\), and \\(11\\), then using the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Modulo 3**  \nSum of digits of \\(74309920\\):  \n\\(7+4+3+0+9+9+2+0 = 34\\).  \n\\(34 \\bmod 3 = 1\\) (since \\(33\\) is divisible by \\(3\\), remainder \\(1\\)).  \nSo:  \n\\(74309920 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Modulo 5**  \nLast digit is \\(0\\), so divisible by \\(5\\).  \nRemainder \\(0\\).  \nSo:  \n\\(74309920 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Modulo 11**  \nAlternating sum of digits (from right to left, starting with + for units digit):\n\nDigits: \\(7,4,3,0,9,9,2,0\\) (left to right).  \nFrom right: \\(0 - 2 + 9 - 9 + 0 - 3 + 4 - 7\\).  \nCompute:  \n\\(0 - 2 = -2\\)  \n\\(-2 + 9 = 7\\)  \n\\(7 - 9 = -2\\)  \n\\(-2 + 0 = -2\\)  \n\\(-2 - 3 = -5\\)  \n\\(-5 + 4 = -1\\)  \n\\(-1 - 7 = -8\\)  \n\nSo alternating sum = \\(-8\\).  \nModulo \\(11\\): \\(-8 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{11}\\) (since \\(-8 + 11 = 3\\)).  \nSo:  \n\\(74309920 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Solve system**  \nWe have:  \n\\(x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\)  \n\\(x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}\\)  \n\\(x \\equiv 3 \\pmod{11}\\)\n\nFrom \\(x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}\\), \\(x = 5k\\).\n\nFrom \\(x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\): \\(5k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\).  \n\\(5 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\\), so \\(2k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\).  \nMultiply inverse of 2 mod 3 (which is 2): \\(k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}\\).  \nSo \\(k = 3m + 2\\).\n\nThen \\(x = 5(3m+2) = 15m + 10\\).\n\nNow use mod 11: \\(15m + 10 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{11}\\).  \n\\(15 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\), so \\(4m + 10 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{11}\\).  \nThus \\(4m \\equiv -7 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\).  \nSo \\(4m \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\).  \nInverse of 4 mod 11 is 3 (since \\(4\\times 3=12\\equiv 1\\)), so \\(m \\equiv 4\\times 3 = 12 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{11}\\).\n\nSo \\(m = 11t + 1\\).\n\nThen \\(x = 15(11t+1) + 10 = 165t + 15 + 10 = 165t + 25\\).\n\n---\n\n**Step 6 \u2013 Conclusion**  \nThe remainder is \\(25\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: 25"
